Page=new Array();Page[0]=new Array("The Help System provides the user with informative overviews, instructive help procedures, examples, notes, tips and screen information.","Click on the following link to view information about the Help System: Using the Help system","Click on the following links to view basic information within the Help System:","Getting Started","License Assistant Wizard","Guide to the User Interface","View Options","Undo and Redo","Content Management","Export and Import","Label Management","Printing","Publishing","Advanced Search and Quick Search","Studio Basics","StudioBasics.htm");
Page[1]=new Array("This comprehensive Help System has been designed and written with all types of users in mind, from system designers and builders to system users. The aim of this help system is to enable the user to use the system effectively and confidently. Use of this help system will aid user performance giving a sense of satisfaction and understanding. ","The Help System provides the user with informative overviews, instructive help procedures, examples, notes, tips and screen information.","The Help System is available at all times. It can be activated by clicking on the F1 button in any area within the software or by selecting the Help menu option from the Main menu bar. <br>For guidance on the different ways to access the Help System, please see the Accessing the Help System help topic for more information.","Click on the following links to view further information about the Help System:","Help dialog","Help viewer","Information Notices","Help System overview","HelpSystemoverview.htm");
Page[2]=new Array("The Help System is available at all times. The user can activate the Help System by clicking on the F1 button in any area within the software or by selecting the Help menu option from the Main menu bar.","To access Help using F1","Whilst anywhere in the software, click on the F1 button.","The Help dialog will appear. Clicking on the F1 button initiates context sensitive help, so that the Help dialog opens on an appropriate page. A help information screen relative to the area of focus will be activated.","The user must have clicked in or be working in an editor to activate help information relative to that area.","To access Help using the Main menu bar","Click on the Help option in the Main menu bar.","A drop-down menu will appear.","Select Help Contents.","The Help dialog will appear. Using the Main menu option initiates general help; the Help dialog will open at the Introduction page. ","Accessing the Help System","AccessingtheHelpSystem.htm");
Page[3]=new Array("The Help System is available at all times. It can be activated by clicking on the F1 button in any area within the software or by selecting the Help menu option from the Main tool bar. For guidance on the different ways to access the Help system, please see the Accessing the Help System help topic.","Once activated, the Help dialog will be displayed:","The Help dialog consists of 3 areas:","The Help System tool bar","The Help Contents and Search area    ","The Help viewer","The Help dialog is an independent screen and can be minimized, maximized, restored down, moved, cropped and closed. For guidance on customizing the Help dialog, please see the Customizing the Help dialog help topic.","Help dialog","Helpdialog.htm");
Page[4]=new Array("The Help dialog is an independent screen and can be minimized, maximized, restored down, moved, cropped and closed. ","To minimize the Help dialog","Click on the @  button.","The Help dialog will be minimized and is accessible from your task bar until the Help dialog has been closed.","To maximize the Help dialog","Click on the @ button.","The Help dialog will now fill your screen.","To restore the Help dialog","Click on the @ button.","The Help dialog will restore down to its normal size.","To move the Help dialog","Click on the silver bar across the top of the Help dialog and drag the dialog to your chosen location on the screen.","The Help dialog can be moved to facilitate a view of the user interface.","To crop the Help dialog","Click on any corner or side of the dialog outline and drag until the dialog is the required size. ","The Help dialog can be cropped to facilitate a view of the user interface.","To close the Help dialog","Click on the @ button.","The Help dialog will now close.","Customizing the Help dialog","CustomizingtheHelpdialog.htm");
Page[5]=new Array("The Help System tool bar is designed to enable the user to navigate through the help system, to print and to customize the page setup for the print.","@  Previous Page &#8211; Allows the user to view the previous page, this works similarly to a back button. The user may only move to pages already viewed in the current session.","@   Next Page &#8211; Allows the users to view the next page, this works similar to a forward button. The user may only move to pages already viewed in the current session.","@  Print &#8211; Allows the user to print the page being viewed. Please see the Print a Help page help topic for more information.","@  Page Setup &#8211; Allows the user to view or edit the page setup of the page being viewed prior to printing. Please see the View or edit the page setup prior to printing help topic for more information.","The Help tool bar","TheHelptoolbar.htm");
Page[6]=new Array("The user can print a Help page.","To print a Help page","Within the Help dialog, ensure that you are viewing the help page you wish to print and click on the @ button.","The Print dialog will appear, similar to the following:","Ensure that the correct printer is selected and click on the OK button.","The help page you are currently viewing will be printed.","Print a Help page","PrintaHelppage.htm");
Page[7]=new Array("The user can view or edit the page setup prior to printing.","To view or edit the page setup prior to printing","Within the Help dialog, ensure that you are viewing the help page you wish to view or edit the page setup and click on the @ button.","The Page Setup dialog will appear, similar to the following:","You have the option to edit the paper size and source, the orientation and the margin limits. Once you have viewed or edited the page setup, click on the OK button.","You may now print the customized page. Please see the Print a Help page help topic for more information.","View or edit the page setup prior to printing","Vieworeditthepagesetuppriortoprinting.htm");
Page[8]=new Array("The Help Contents and Search area enables the user to navigate through the help system and to search for keywords within the help system.","There are 2 windows within the Contents and Search area of the Help system:","The Contents window in Help.","The Search window in Help.","Help Contents and Search area","HelpContentsandSearcharea.htm");
Page[9]=new Array("The Contents window displays the structure of the help system. ","The help system is made up of books and pages.","@  This icon signifies a book.","@ This icon signifies an opened book, its pages will be displayed beneath it.","@  This icon signifies a page.","Pages are stored in books that are ordered to reflect the steps a system designer, system builder or a system user may need to take in order to understand, create or use the system. A book can contain more books.","When the user double clicks on a book icon, its pages will be displayed. The user can then view each help page within that book. Please see the View a Help page help topic for further information.","The user can also use the following to open or close books:"," @ Click on this icon to open a book."," @ Click on this icon to close a book.","Contents window in Help","ContentswindowinHelp.htm");
Page[10]=new Array("Once in the Help dialog, the user can view Help pages.","To view a Help page","Within the Help dialog and with the contents window selected, double click on the required book @ icon or click on the @ icon.","Click on the required page icon.","The page will now appear in the Help viewer area. Use the @ and @  icons in the Help tool bar to move to previous or next pages within the book. You may only move through pages you have already viewed in your current session. To view a new page, repeat step 1 and 2.","View a Help page","ViewaHelppage.htm");
Page[11]=new Array("The Search window enables the user to search for a key word or words within the help system. Using the search will display all the help pages where that word is used, either in the title, or within the help page content. &nbsp;This is the widest search available.","To search for a key word or words, please see the Search for a word within Help help topic for further information.","Search window in Help","SearchwindowinHelp.htm");
Page[12]=new Array("The Search window enables the user to search for a key word or words within the help system. Using the search will display all the help pages where that word is used, either in the title, or within the help page content. &nbsp;This is the widest search available.","To search for a word within Help","Within the Help dialog and with the Search window selected, type a word or words relating to the information you wish to find into the Find field.","Press Enter on your keyboard.","The Search window will display all pages with the word or words within it and the Help viewer will display the help page at the top of the list. You can view each page in the list by clicking on the page description in the Search window.","Search for a word within Help","SearchforawordwithinHelp.htm");
Page[13]=new Array("The Help viewer allows the user to view any selected help pages within the help system. The Help viewer is read only; however, clicking on a link within a page will take the user to another appropriate help page.","To view a Help page, please see the View a Help page help topic.","Help viewer","Helpviewer.htm");
Page[14]=new Array("The help system provides the user with information notices. These notices are iconised and highlighted pieces of information intended to provide the user with extra information.","There are 4 types of Information notices used within the help system:","Note","This information notice provides the user with extra information. ","Note example:","Only complete quarters (contained within the analysis period) will be included in the output.","Tip","This information notice provides the user with information to speed up a process or to make it easier.","Tip example:","The BC uses 'IP' as a marker to indicate that the user specifies an IP address other than the default. The marker is not case sensitive, 'ip' or 'Ip' can be used as well.","Caution","This information notice provides the user with information on the consequence of an action or the consequence of the lack of an action.","Caution example:","The SIA displays errors and discontinues working if the user does not specify any of the above mentioned attributes.","Example","This information notice provides the user with an example of a concept or instruction that has just been explained.","Example example:","A sample suite contains two child suites: Test and Production. The Production child suite contains one child suite: Scorecard. Executing 'Sample' causes the server to run all the reports in all the four suites. Executing 'Production' causes the server to run all of the reports in the 'Production' and 'Scorecard' suites. Executing 'Scorecard' runs only the reports in the 'Scorecard' suite. Executing 'Test' runs only the reports in the 'Test' suite.","Information Notices","InformationNotices.htm");
Page[15]=new Array("This section provides guidance on getting started in the software. Once you have installed the software it can be difficult to know what to do next.","Please see the following sections for guidance;","Security - for information on setting up a new user with the appropriate security profile. ","Licensing - for information on the trial license and requesting and activating a license.","User Interface - for more information on the interface.","Content Management - for information on how to import a new folder/solution template to help you get started.","Export/Import  - for information on how to import a pre-defined solution.","Getting Started overview","GettingStartedoverview.htm");
Page[16]=new Array("Security governs the access and permissions that a user has within the software.","Following installation of the software, to be able to work within the software you must first create a new user with the appropriate security profile. ","Every user must have a user account and can be assigned specific roles within that account. Each role is assigned permissions that determine the access that the user has to various components in the business area.","For further information on Security, please see the Security overview.","Security - getting started","Security-gettingstarted.htm");
Page[17]=new Array("When the software is first installed it will be installed with a 14 day trial license. The License Assistant Wizard enables the user to request a new license or activate a new license.","The trial license will expire in 14 days and you will not be warned prior to expiry of the license. ","If a user is installing a minor release upgrade to a previously licensed version, they are not required to apply for a new license. The user can reactivate the existing license. ","The License Assistant Wizard can be accessed at any time and displays the number of days you have remaining on your trial period. ","Licensing - getting started","Licensing-gettingstarted.htm");
Page[18]=new Array("When the software is first installed it will be installed with a 14 day trial license. The License Assistant Wizard enables the user to request a new license or activate a new license.","To request a new license a registration request will need to be completed, once you have received a license you will need to complete the registration by activating the license.","License Assistant overview","LicenseAssistantoverview.htm");
Page[19]=new Array("When the software is first installed it will be installed with a 14 day trial license. The License Assistant Wizard enables the user to request a new license or activate a new license.","To request a new license a registration request will need to be completed, once you have received a license you will need to complete the registration by activating the license.","To request a new License ","In the Main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar, and select License Assistant Wizard. The Introduction screen of the License Assistant Wizard will be launched. ","Click on the Next button. The Registration and Activation screen will be opened. ","Select the Request license or License extension radio button. ","Click on the Next button.","The Product Licensing Information screen will be initiated.","Within the Edition drop down box, select the edition that is appropriate for your implementation.<br>An edition is a combination of capability and licensing that together with security privileges will give you the access you require. ","Click on the Next button.","The License type page will be launched.","Select Standalone or Network license.","For a Network license, select the maximum number of concurrent users and press the '...' button. Enter the name or the IP of the network licensing server and click on the OK button. If the name or IP of the network licensing server is correct and the server is available then the name or the IP address of the licensing server will be displayed in the License server field.","Click on the Next button. The Customer Information screen will be launched. ","Fully complete the registration information ensuring that you completely fill in those boxes that have a * next to them. ","Click on the Next button. The Save Registration Information screen will be launched. ","Click on the Browse button to save the file to a location of your choice. You will need to e-mail this file. ","Click on the Next button. The Comments screen will be launched. ","Enter any comments you require. ","Click on the Finish button. The Summary screen will be launched. It will provide you with the location of the file you have just saved and the Email address to which you should send your registration file. ","Click on the Close button. ","Email the registration file to the given Email address (step 18).","Request a new license","Requestanewlicense.htm");
Page[20]=new Array("When the software is first installed it will be installed with a 14 day trial license. The License Assistant Wizard enables the user to request a new license or activate a new license.","Before activating a licence, ensure that the studio is running in the same mode as the licence being activated. For example, if you are activating a network licence, the studio needs to be running in Network licence mode. <br>The licence mode can be altered by selecting the Change Preferences radio button within the License Assistant Wizard.","To request a new license a registration request will need to be completed. Once the license code file has been received and saved, the user will need to complete the registration by activating the license.","To activate a new License","Request a new license.","When you have received the license code file, save this to a local drive.","In the Main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar, and select License Assistant Wizard. The Introduction screen of the License Assistant Wizard will be launched.","Click on the Next button. The Registration and Activation screen will be opened.","Select the Activate license radio button.","Click on the Next button. The License File Location screen will be launched.","Click on the Browse button to launch the Open dialog from where you will be able to locate the license code file (saved in step 2).","Highlight the license code file and click on the Open button. The Open dialog will close and place the full path name for the license you have selected in the License File Location screen.","Click on the Next button.","The License type page will be opened.","Select the type of the license &#8211; Standalone or Network","For a network license click on the &#8216;...&#8217; button. Enter the name or IP address of the network license server. Press Enter or click on the OK button to close the network licensing server dialog. If the name or IP of the network licensing server is correct and the server is available then the name or the IP address of the licensing server will be displayed in the License server field. ","Click on the Next button.","Restart Prompt page will be activated.","Select the restart now or the restart later option. Please note: license will be activated on restart.","Click on the Finish button. The Summary screen will be launched informing you that you have successfully activated the license.","Click on the Close button.","You will now be licensed to use the software.","Activate a new license","Activateanewlicense.htm");
Page[21]=new Array("When the software is first installed it will be installed with a 14 day trial license. The License Assistant Wizard enables the user to request a new license or activate a new license.","To request a new license a registration request will need to be completed, once you have received a license you will need to complete the registration by activating the license.","A user can change license preferences.","To change license preferences ","In the Main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar, and select License Assistant Wizard. The Introduction screen of the License Assistant Wizard will be launched. ","Click on the Next button.The Registration and Activation screen will be opened. ","Select the Change preferences radio button. ","Click on the Next button.","The License type page will be opened.","Select the type of the license &#8211; Standalone or Network.","For a network license click on the  &#8216;...&#8217; button. Enter the name or IP address of the network license server. Press Enter or click on the OK button to close the network licensing server dialog. If the name or IP of the network licensing server is correct and the server is available then the name or the IP address of the licensing server will be displayed in the Licence server field. ","Click on the Next button.","The Restart Prompt page will be activated.","Select the restart now or the restart later option. Please note: license will be activated on restart.","Click on the Finish button. The Summary screen will be launched informing you that you have successfully activated the license. ","Click on the Close button. ","Change license preferences","Changelicensepreferences.htm");
Page[22]=new Array("The software is an architectural framework designed to support a seamlessly integrated suite of business-user applications that share common modules and business definitions.","The software is built in Java and delivers what is known as a rich-client platform; it is easy to install and can be automatically updated. It offers a completely flexible solution structure which solution owners can work within to create unique perspectives for other system users. The software gives the user the ability to:","Create Repositories","Create Domains","Create Solutions","Create a Solution structure","Edit the Global Data Universe including logical data sources, characteristics and physical definitions","Design and create components required to build a solution","The User Interface enables the user to design and build the system. ","The User Interface consists of six areas:","The Main menu bar","The Main tool bar","The Main editor","The Explorer area","The Output area","The Palette area","Please see the Security Help topics for information on the permissions required to perform certain actions.","The user can customize the User Interface view. Please see the User Interface view options overview help page for more information on this.","User Interface overview","UserInterfaceoverview.htm");
Page[23]=new Array("The Main menu bar works in the same way as any Main menu bar. It is located across the top of the interface.","To use the Main menu bar","In the Main system view, click on an option in the Main menu bar.","A drop-down list will appear. ","Select a further option from the drop-down list.","The options available in the menu bar will be dependant on the version of software the user is running and where in the software the user session is active.","The Search bar is also located in the main menu bar.","@ Quick Search in the system - Allows the user to initiate a quick search for system components, action names, option names, type names etc.","Main menu bar","Mainmenubar.htm");
Page[24]=new Array("The Main tool bar enables the user to save work, save changes, cut, copy and paste. It also enables the user to undo and redo actions, monitor memory usage, carry out a quick search and validate a component. It is located directly below the Main menu bar in the user interface.","The following tools are displayed on the tool bar:","@ Validate - Allows the user to validate the component in focus in the Main editor.","@ Save - Allows the user to save changes.","@ Save all files - Allows the user to save all files.","@ Cut - Allows the user to cut an object and place it into memory.","@ Copy - Allows the user to copy an object into memory.","@ Paste - Allows the user to paste an object that has been stored in memory.","@ Undo - Allows the user to undo actions made in text editors and table editors. ","@ Redo - Allows the user to redo actions made in text editors and table editors.","@ Memory monitor - Allows the user to monitor memory usage. This shows the amount of memory currently being used by the application and the total amount of memory allocated to the application.","@ Snapshot - This allows the user to generate a snapshot of memory usage which can be saved and sent to Experian support for further analysis. Click to start the capture process and then click to stop the process and save the data.","If all options do not appear available to the user, the user can modify the Main tool bar if required.","Main tool bar","Maintoolbar.htm");
Page[25]=new Array("The Main tool bar enables the user to save work, save changes, cut, copy and paste. It also enables the user to undo and redo actions, monitor memory usage and carry out a quick search. It is located directly below the Main menu bar in the user interface. If all options do not appear available to the user, the user may modify the Main tool bar.","To modify the Main tool bar","In the main system view, click on the View option in the Main menu bar and select Toolbars. ","Click on the listed tools to add or remove them from the tool bar display.","The Main menu tool bar will display accordingly.","Modify the Main tool bar","ModifytheMaintoolbar.htm");
Page[26]=new Array("By default, the Main editor is displayed in the middle of the user interface.","The Main editor is used to edit components. When a component is selected, it opens for editing in the Main editor. The layout of the windows displayed in this editor changes significantly dependant on the component open in the Main editor.","The Main editor is where the majority of the creating, editing and defining will take place. All new components are configured in the Main editor.","The user can have many components open in the main editor, and can change the component in view by clicking on the appropriate window tab at the top of the Main editor. ","Main editor","Maineditor.htm");
Page[27]=new Array("By default, the Explorer area is displayed down the left hand side of the User Interface.","The Explorer area houses the following windows:","The Explorer window. ","The Server Connections Manager window.","The Strategy Viewer window.  Please see the Strategy Viewer window help topic for more information on this.","The Navigator window. ","The Satellite View window. ","The Where Used window.","All of the windows (with the exception of the Satellite View window) can be initiated from the Main menu bar.","The Satellite View window will only be displayed when the user is working in the Decision Process Flow editor, Decision Setter editor or publishing. ","Explorer area","Explorerarea.htm");
Page[28]=new Array("The Explorer is the area of the user interface where Repositories, Domains, Solutions, Folders and Components are stored and displayed. This is the area in which the hierarchical tree structure of the system can be created and maintained.","The Explorer window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software, the Explorer window will not be displayed. It can be initiated from the Main menu bar. Once initiated, it will display on the left hand side of the interface.","Explorer overview","Exploreroverview.htm");
Page[29]=new Array("The Explorer window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software the Explorer window will not be displayed. It can be initiated from the Main menu bar. Once initiated, it will display on the left hand side of the interface. If closed and reopened it will display in its default position.","The Explorer window consists of:","The Explorer tool bar","The Hierarchical tree structure area","The Explorer view bar","If the Explorer window is not visible in the User Interface, it can be initiated at any time. Please see initiate the Explorer window help topic for more information on this.","The Explorer window will display only areas for which the user has permissions.","The text colouring used in the hierarchical tree structure area of the Explorer window varies depending on where the item is located; please see the following descriptions:","Normal text - Item is located in the Shared Area only","Blue text - Item is located in the User Area and also in the Shared Area","Green text - Item is located in the User Area only","Red text - Item is located both in user and shared area but with an active hide flag  ","Red Strikethrough text - Item is located in the shared area only but with an active hide flag ","The above colours are the default colours; the user can  customise the colouring of the text displayed in the Explorer window if required.","Greyed out text - Item is not available to the user in the studio that they currently have running.","Explorer window","Explorerwindow.htm");
Page[30]=new Array("If the Explorer window is not visible in the user interface the user can initiate this at any time.","To initiate the Explorer window","In the main system view, click on the Window option in the Main menu bar and select Explorer.","The Explorer window will now display in its predefined location in the user interface.","You can drag and drop the Explorer window to any preferred location. Please see the Customize the User Interface help page for more information on this.","Initiate the Explorer window","InitiatetheExplorerwindow.htm");
Page[31]=new Array("The Explorer window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software, the Explorer window will not be displayed. It can be  initiated from the Main menu bar. Once initiated, it will display on the left hand side of the interface. ","The Explorer window consists of a tool bar, the hierarchical tree structure area and the Explorer view bar.","The hierarchical tree structure area displays the following:","Repositories - A Repository is used to hold and display a secure and persisted copy of the client&#8217;s system(s) which can be accessed and updated by the users of the Studio applications. These users may be collaborating on changes to shared systems or may be working alongside each other in separate areas of a system (or on separate systems); the Repository provides an archive and audit trail of changes made by these users during the lifetime of the systems. There are 3 types of Repository by default:"," @Content repository "," @Reporting repository "," @ Solution repository ","@  Domains - A Repository may contain one or more Domains, each of which can contain one or more Solutions. User details and access permissions operate at Repository level, and a user&#8217;s role-based permissions may therefore span Domains within the Repository, or be confined within a single Domain, as required. Many clients, particularly those with only a single Solution, or a small number of Solutions, will generally have a single Domain within their Repository. For enterprise-level clients, or for Delivery Centres working on multiple Solutions for many clients, the Domain provides a useful mechanism for grouping sets of Solutions that logically belong together (and conversely to separate / isolate them from other Solutions / groups of Solutions). ","@ Solutions - A Solution is a level by which the contents of Domains can be further divided. Solutions are held within a domain and the content of a solution can be viewed in the Explorer window.","@  Folders - Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained in a solution. Dependant on permissions, a user can view the contents of a folder, add a folder or delete a folder. Folders can contain many different types of components, however for ease of location it is recommended that they are used to group components of a similar type; for example, segmentation devices, decision components and decision process flows etc Manage allowed component types allows the user to determine which components should be held in which folders. Folders are stored in the Explorer window.","Components - A component is an entity within a Solution that carries out a particular business function. Examples include Decision Process Flows, Scorecards, Logical Data Source etc. Each type of component has its own icon. Components are stored in Folders within the Explorer window.","The text used in the hierarchical tree structure area of the Explorer window varies, please see Text colours in the Explorer window help topic for more information.","Hierarchical tree structure of the system","Hierarchicaltreestructureofthesystem.htm");
Page[32]=new Array("The Explorer window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software the Explorer window will not be displayed. It can be initiated from the Main menu bar. Once initiated, it will display on the left hand side of the interface. ","The Explorer window consists of a tool bar, the hierarchical tree structure area and the Explorer view bar.","The Explorer tool bar is only visible whilst in Explorer view and enables the user tomanipulate the view of the hierarchical tree structure of the system. ","If the user has stepped in to a solution or folder level, the user can select multi components or multi folders in Explorer. If the user has not stepped in to a solution or folder level, the multi-selection is not available.","@ Home - Click on this icon to view all repositories and their contents in the Explorer window.","@ Step into - Highlight a repository, a domain, a solution or a folder and then click on this icon to view only this and its contents in the Explorer window. ","For example, on highlighting a solution, clicking on the Step into icon will mean you have a view of the solution only and the multi select function can be used:","The multi select function is only available when the solution or folder have been stepped into.","@ Step back - Click on this icon to view the parent folder, solution, domain or repository and its content.","@ Collapse all - Highlight a Solution or a Folder and then click on this icon to close the folder or solution you have selected and all its child folders. Nothing will be displayed.","@ Expand all - Highlight a Solution or a Folder and then click on this icon to open the folder or solution you have selected and all its child folders.  All the components contained in the folders will be displayed in the Explorer Window.","Explorer tool bar","Explorertoolbar.htm");
Page[33]=new Array("The Explorer window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software the Explorer window will not be displayed. It can be  initiated from the Main menu bar. Once initiated, it will display on the left hand side of the interface. ","The Explorer window consists of a tool bar, the hierarchical tree structure area and the Explorer view bar.","The Explorer view bar is displayed at the bottom of the Explorer window.","The icons allow the user to choose different views of the hierarchical tree structure of the system.","@  Explorer view (default view) - Click on this icon to display the hierarchical structure of the repository. In this view, components are organised in folders in alphabetical order.","@  Component Types view - Click on this icon to display components in groups depending on types. The component types that are present in the selected repository are displayed in a list.","@  Recently Changed view - Click on this icon to display only those components that have changed within the past week, regardless of the user.","@  Show/Hide Obsolete - Click on this icon to show or hide components in the Explorer window. Components that have been checked in and hidden will display in red with a strikethrough. A user can choose to show a component or hide a component in the Explorer window. ","@  My Work view - Click on this icon to display only those components that the user has created or modified. Components in the local and shared areas will be displayed. ","@  Favourite view - Click on this icon to display only those components that the user has marked as favourite. For more information, refer to the Mark a component as favourite topic.","You can use the @ and the @ icons to collapseand expandthe folders.","Explorer view bar","Explorerviewbar.htm");
Page[34]=new Array("The text colouring used in the hierarchical tree structure area of the Explorer window varies depending on where the item is located; please see the following descriptions:","Normal text - Item is located in the Shared Area only","Blue text - Item is located in the User Area and also in the Shared Area","Green text - Item is located in the User Area only","Red text - Item is located both in user and shared area but with an active hide flag  ","Red Strikethrough text - Item is located in the shared area only but with an active hide flag ","The above colours are the default colours; the user can customise the colouring of the text displayed in the Explorer window if required.","Greyed out text - Item is not available to the user in the studio that they currently have running.","Text colours in the Explorer window","TextcoloursintheExplorerwindow.htm");
Page[35]=new Array("The text colouring used in the hierarchical tree structure area of the Explorer window varies depending on where the item is located. The user can customise the text colouring if required.","To customise the text colouring in the Explorer window","In the Main system view, click on the Tools option in the Main menu bar.","A drop-down list will appear.","Select Options.","The Options dialog will be initiated.","Click on the Explorer tab.","In the Colour of Components in... field, click on the @ next to the location you wish to customise the colour for.","The Select the color to use... dialog will be initiated.","In the Swatches tab, click on the required colour in the colour grid. A sample of  text in the chosen colour will be displayed in the preview field of the dialog.","Click on the OK button.","The Select the color to use... dialog will close."," In the Options dialog, click on the OK button.","The customisation will be activated immediately.","Customise the text coloring in the Explorer window","CustomisethetextcoloringintheExplorerwindow.htm");
Page[36]=new Array("A Repository is used to hold a secure and persisted copy of the client&#8217;s system(s) which can be accessed and updated by the users of the Studio applications. These users may be collaborating on changes to shared systems or may be working alongside each other in separate areas of a system (or on separate systems); the Repository provides an archive and audit trail of changes made by these users during the lifetime of the systems."," @","Repositories are displayed in the Server Connections Manager window and in the Explorer window. ","The Repository is also the location from which collections of users' changes will be coordinated and collated into deployment packages (see Label Management).","Repositories are displayed with the following icons:","@Content repository ","@Reporting repository ","@ Solution repository ","The user can create as many repositories as is required and can connect to several repositories thanks to the single sign on feature. A user may have access to multiple repositories, but must be connected to a repository to work on the components within it.","A Repository is the receptacle where the Domains and the Solutions are stored.","Repository overview","Repositoryoverview.htm");
Page[37]=new Array("A repository is used to hold a secure and persisted copy of the client&#8217;s system(s). Repositories are displayed in the Server Manager Connections window. The contents of the repository can be viewed and accessed from the Explorer window.","A user with adequate permissions can log in to a repository as required. The user can work in a repository only when connected to it. ","To connect to a repository","In the Explorer window, right click on the appropriate repository. ","Select Connect.","You can also double click on the Repository to connect.","The Repository name turns blue to show that you are connected to it. Click on the @ icon to expand the list of domains within the repository.","Connect to a repository","Connecttoarepository.htm");
Page[38]=new Array("A repository is used to hold a secure and persisted copy of the client&#8217;s system(s). Repositories are displayed in the Server Manager Connections window. The contents of the repository can be viewed and accessed from the Explorer window.","A user with adequate permissions can connect to a repository as required. The user can work in a repository only when connected to it. Once connected to a repository, the user must open it to view the domains, solutions, folders and components stored within it.","To open a repository","You must first connect to a repository.","In the Explorer window, highlight the required repository and click on the @ icon.","The domains within the repository will now be displayed in the Explorer window. You can now load a domain.","Clicking on the @  to the left of the repository icon in the Explorer window will expand a repository.","Open a repository","Openarepository.htm");
Page[39]=new Array("A repository is used to hold a secure and persisted copy of the client&#8217;s system(s). Repositories are displayed in the Server Manager Connections window. The contents of the repository can be viewed and accessed from the Explorer window.","A user with adequate permissions can connect to a repository as required. The user can work in a repository only when connected to it. ","The user can disconnect from repositories as required.","To disconnect from a repository","In the Explorer window, right click on the Repository you wish to disconnect from.","Select Disconnect. ","The repository name turns grey which means that you are disconnected from the repository.","Disconnect from a repository","Disconnectfromarepository.htm");
Page[40]=new Array("A Repository may contain one or more Domains, each of which can contain one or more Solutions. User details and access permissions operate at repository level, and a user's role-based permissions may therefore span domains within the repository, or be confined within a single domain, as required. ","Many clients, particularly those with only a single solution, or a small number of solutions, will generally have a single domain within their repository. For enterprise-level clients, or for delivery centres working on multiple solutions for many clients, the domain provides a useful mechanism for grouping sets of solutions that logically belong together (and conversely to separate / isolate them from other solutions / groups of solutions). ","A Domain is displayed with the @ icon and can be viewed, navigated to, added, deleted and renamed in the Explorer window. ","Domain overview","Domainoverview.htm");
Page[41]=new Array("The New dialog enables a user to add a new domain to a repository.","Please see the Add an empty domain and the Add a pre-configured domain help topic for information on how to proceed.","New Domain dialog","NewDomaindialog.htm");
Page[42]=new Array("The Add domain dialog enables a user to add a domain to a repository.","Please see the Add a domain help topic for information on how to proceed.","Add domain dialog","Adddomaindialog.htm");
Page[43]=new Array("A Repository may contain one or more Domains, each of which can contain one or more Solutions.","Domains are stored and displayed within a repository in the Explorer window. The user can add an empty or pre-configured domain.","To add an empty domain","In the Explorer window, right click on the required repository.","Select New.","In the New dialog, select Empty domain and click on the OK button.","In the Add domain dialog, enter a name for the domain.","Click on the OK button.","The new domain will be listed within the selected repository. You may now add a solution to the domain.","Add an empty domain","Addanemptydomain.htm");
Page[44]=new Array("A Repository may contain one or more Domains, each of which can contain one or more Solutions.","Domains are stored and displayed within a repository in the Explorer window. The user can add an empty domain or a pre-configured domain to a repository.","To enable repository and domain level export, additional information has been added in the export process, storing the domain details within the XML file. Therefore, older exports without the correct domain details (prior to 2.2) will only be supported from a solution level import (and are therefore not supported at repository / domain level import as it can not validate the domain information).","If there is a file mismatch, the following error message will be given:","It is recommended that any XML (pre v2.2) systems are imported into the new software via the solution node by an architect and then re-exported to capture this additional information within the export file. This will enable them to be imported from a repository or domain level.","To add a pre-configured domain","In the Explorer window, right click on the required repository.","Select New.","In the New dialog, select Pre-configured domain and click on the OK button.","The Import wizard will be initiated.","The first screen, Select import source, is displayed. Locate and select the xml file to import.","From the Files of type field, select Experian Proprietary Format: ","Click on the Next button to display the second screen of the Import wizard, View import file. Review the components and folder structure to be imported.","Click on the Next button to display the third screen of the Import wizard, Existing components. The screen will display a list of any components among those you are attempting to import that are already in the target solution. ","If you want to import the existing components, you must import them into your user area by checking the Import tickbox:","If you do not specify that the existing components are to be imported into your user area, they will not be imported.","If all the components already exist in the target solution, you will be unable to continue the import process until you check the tickbox; the following message will be displayed:","Click on the Next button to display the fourth screen of the Import wizard, Confirm choices. Review the name and the location of the imported file. ","Unless all components are to be imported into the user domain, the Comments field is mandatory; type a relevant comment. The comment is for users who want to know why a component was imported and it appears in the History of a component in the shared domain, in the Comments column.","The Label field is an optional field (A label is a method of grouping objects together. The label represents a version of the objects as a collective group). ","Click on the Next button to display the fifth screen of the wizard, Import job summary.","The process will now be sent for remote execution. You can specify that the Job Submission Console will launch automatically when you exit the wizard by clicking in the Launch Job Submission Console tickbox.","Click on the Finish button.","The new domain will be listed within the selected repository. You may now add an empty solution or add a pre-configured solution to the domain.","Add a pre-configured domain","Addapre-configureddomain.htm");
Page[45]=new Array("A Repository may contain one or more Domains, each of which can contain one or more Solutions.","Domains are stored and displayed within a repository in the Explorer window.","To rename a domain","In the Explorer window, right click on the domain you want to rename.","Select Rename.","In the Rename dialog, type the new name and click on the OK button.","The system will make sure that the name is unique within the repository and apply the name to the domain.","Rename a domain","Renameadomain.htm");
Page[46]=new Array("A Repository may contain one or more Domains, each of which can contain one or more Solutions.","Domains are stored and displayed within a repository in the Explorer window.","To navigate to a domain","You must first Log into a Repository.","In the Explorer window, highlight the required repository and click on the @ icon.","The domains within the repository will now be displayed in the Explorer window.","Highlight the required domain and click on the @ icon.","The domain is now loaded and the solutions within the domain will now be displayed. You can now load a solution.","Clicking on the @  to the left of the domain icon in the Explorer window will expand the domain.","Navigate to a domain","Navigatetoadomain.htm");
Page[47]=new Array("A Repository may contain one or more Domains, each of which can contain one or more Solutions.","Domains are stored and displayed within a repository in the Explorer window. ","The removal of a domain will mean deletion of its content.","A user must have the Architect role to remove a domain.","To remove a domain","In the Explorer window, right click on the domain that you want to remove.","Select Remove.","In the Question dialog, click on the Yes button to confirm the removal request.","The domain will be removed.","Remove a domain","Removeadomain.htm");
Page[48]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of domains can be further divided. Some examples could include solutions that:","are composed from purely decisioning capability and content, or purely operational capability and content, or from a combination of both","are organised differently based on business objectives and solution scope","cover multiple work streams such as origination, customer management and reporting","are multi-country solutions designed with the capability to isolate country specifics","manage multiple credit products and associated components with the potential for cross product activities such as cross-selling","The publishing mechanism that allows sharing of components operates within the solution boundary; for example, definitions of data models and layouts can be located in a folder and published for use within other parts of the solution, but not within other Solutions.","A Solution is represented with the @ icon and can be viewed, added, deleted, renamed and loaded in the Explorer window.","The user can import a previously exported component, folder or solution along with any dependent components and folder structures.","The user can export a component, folder or solution along with any dependant components and folder structures.","Solution overview","Solutionoverview.htm");
Page[49]=new Array("The New dialog enables a user to add a new solution to a domain.","Please see the Add an empty solution and the Add a pre-configured solution help topic for information on how to proceed.","New solution dialog","Newsolutiondialog.htm");
Page[50]=new Array("The Add solution dialog enables a user to add a solution to a domain.","Please see the Add an empty solution help topic for information on how to proceed.","Add solution dialog","Addsolutiondialog.htm");
Page[51]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of Domains can be further divided.","Solutions are stored and displayed within a domain in the Explorer window. The user can add an empty solution or a pre-configured solution.","To add an empty solution","In the Explorer window, right click on the domain within which you want to add the new solution.","Select New.","In the New dialog, select Empty solution and click on the OK button.","Select Add solution.","In the Add solution dialog, type the name of the new solution.","Click on the OK button.","The solution will be added to the domain.","Add an empty solution","Addanemptysolution.htm");
Page[52]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of domains can be further divided.","Solutions are stored and displayed within a domain in the Explorer window. The user can add an empty solution or a pre-configured solution to a domain.","To add a pre-configured solution","You must have a target solution loaded prior to commencing.","In the Explorer window, right click on the required domain.","Select New.","In the New dialog, select Pre-configured solution and click on the OK button.","The Import wizard will be initiated.","The first screen, Select import source, is displayed. Locate and select the xml file to import.","From the Files of type field, select Experian Proprietary Format: ","Click on the Next button to display the second screen of the Import wizard, View import file. Review the components and folder structure to be imported.","Click on the Next button to display the third screen of the Import wizard, Existing components. The screen will display a list of any components among those you are attempting to import that are already in the target solution. ","If you want to import the existing components, you must import them into your user area by checking the Import tickbox:","If you do not specify that the existing components are to be imported into your user area, they will not be imported.","If all the components already exist in the target solution, you will be unable to continue the import process until you check the tickbox; the following message will be displayed:","Click on the Next button to display the fourth screen of the Import wizard, Confirm choices. Review the name and the location of the imported file. ","Unless all components are to be imported into the user domain, the Comments field is mandatory; type a relevant comment. The comment is for users who want to know why a component was imported and it appears in the History of a component in the shared domain, in the Comments column.","The Label field is an optional field. ","Click on the Next button to display the fifth screen of the wizard, Import job summary.","The process will now be sent for remote execution. You can specify that the Job Submission Console will launch automatically when you exit the wizard by clicking in the Launch Job Submission Console tickbox.","Click on the Finish button.","The new solution will be listed within the selected domain. ","Add a pre-configured solution","Addapre-configuredsolution.htm");
Page[53]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of Domains can be further divided.","Solutions are stored and displayed within a domain in the Explorer window.","To close a solution","In the Explorer window, right click on the solution you want to close.","Select Close solution.","The solution will be closed.","Close a solution","Closeasolution.htm");
Page[54]=new Array("A Solution Signature is a unique identity given to a solution and is used at runtime as an &#8216;internal&#8217; password to ensure that the process flow being executed is for the correct client solution. The solution signature is also used to gain access to view deployed strategy contents within the Deployed Strategy Viewer.","The user is prompted to enter the solution signature during the execution of already deployed jobs. This additional security feature ensures that the person deploying a strategy is authorised by the solution architect to carry out this kind of action.","At solution design stage, there is no need to enter the signature to carry out designing actions. ","To add a solution signature","In the Explorer window, right click on the loaded solution to which you want to add the signature. ","Select Add solution signature.","In the Add Signature dialog, type the signature into the Signature field.","The solution signature is case sensitive and is limited to 8 characters in length.","Click on the OK button.","The signature will be applied to the solution.","A signature can only be assigned to a client system by a user who has 'Architect' access rights.","Add a signature to a solution","Addasignaturetoasolution.htm");
Page[55]=new Array("The Add Signature dialog enables the user to type the signature for the solution.","A Solution Signature is a unique identity given to a solution and is used at runtime as an 'internal' password to ensure that the correct process flows are being executed for the correct client solution.","The solution signature is case sensitive and is limited to 8 characters in length.","Add Signature dialog","AddSignaturedialog.htm");
Page[56]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of Domains can be further divided.","To rename a solution","In the Explorer window, right click on the solution you wish to rename.","Select Rename.","In the Rename dialog, type the new name in the New name field.","Click on the OK button.","The system will check to ensure that this name is unique in the domain and rename the solution.","Rename a solution","Renameasolution.htm");
Page[57]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of Domains can be further divided.","Solutions are stored and displayed within a domain in the Explorer window.","To load a solution","You must first navigate to a domain.","In the Explorer window, highlight the required domain and click on the @ icon.","The solutions within the domain will now be displayed.","Right click on the required solution and select Load solution.","You can also double click on the Solution to connect.","You can now click on  the @ icon to open the Solution. ","Clicking on the @ icon to the left of the solution icon in the Explorer window will expand the solution.","Load a solution","Loadasolution.htm");
Page[58]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of Domains can be further divided.","Solutions are stored and displayed within a domain in the Explorer window. ","The removal of a solution will mean deletion of its content.","A user must have the Architect role to remove a solution.","To remove a solution","In the Explorer window, right click on the solution that you wish to remove.","Select Remove.","In the Question dialog, click on the Yes button to confirm the removal request.","The solution will be removed from the domain.","Remove a solution","Removeasolution.htm");
Page[59]=new Array("A Solution is a level by which the contents of Domains can be further divided.","Solutions are stored and displayed within a domain in the Explorer window.","When a user with architect access is creating folders or editing the publishing rules within a solution, a lock token is put on the solution. ","If another user with the same access tries to create folders or edit the publishing rules within the locked solution, a warning dialog will be initiated. This is expected behaviour.","However, if the server shuts down abnormally whilst the lock token is in place, or if a user with architect access has left a session open in editing mode in error, other users with architect access will continue to face the Warning dialog. If this is the case, the solution may be unlocked for editing. Only a user with Solution Administrator access will be able to unlock a locked solution.","Please note that this is a maintenance operation only and not a usual business action. This should be used in extreme cases only.","To unlock a solution for editing","In the Explorer window, right click on the locked solution.","Select Unlock.","You may now create folders or edit the publishing rules within the solution.","Unlock a locked solution for editing","Unlockalockedsolutionforediting.htm");
Page[60]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The user may validate a Solution from the Explorer window.","To validate a Solution","In the Explorer window, select the Solution that you wish to validate.","Right click and select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validate a Solution","ValidateaSolution.htm");
Page[61]=new Array("Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained within a solution. Folders can contain many different types of components. It makes things easier to find if components of a similar type are grouped together, for example; segmentation devices, decision process flows, etc. Folders are stored in the shared area and displayed in the Explorer window. ","A folder is displayed with the @ icon and can be viewed, added, deleted, renamed and published in the Explorer window. A folder can not be deleted if it contains components which are located in the shared repository. All actions within folders can be performed by a user with Architect access rights.","The user can define which components will be allowed in the folders. Please see the manage allowed components types help page for more information on this topic.Specific access rights to folders can be assigned to individual users or to user groups.","The publishing mechanism within folders allows for the sharing of components within the solution boundary, for example; definitions of data models and layouts can be located in a folder and published for use within other parts of the solution, but not within other solutions; please see the Publishing overview for more information. ","The user can import a previously exported component, folder or solution along with any dependent components and folder structures.","The user can export a component, folder or solution along with any dependant components and folder structures.","Folder overview","Folderoverview.htm");
Page[62]=new Array("The Add folder dialog enables a user to add a folder to a solution or another folder.","The dialog consists of:","Name field - the user must type a name for the folder.","Categories field - the user can select a pre-defined set of components for any particular system by selecting a specific category from the drop-down list.","Left field - displays the pre-defined set of components within the selected category.","Right field: Allowed component types - displays the selected allowed component types.","&gt;  -  use this to add a selected component from the left field to the allowed component types.","&gt;&gt; -  use this to add all components from the left field to the allowed component types.","&lt;  -  use this to remove a selected component from the allowed component types.","&lt;&lt; -  use this to remove all components from the allowed component types.","Copy from parent - use this to copy all component types from the parent of the selected folder (copying from parent will also copy the licence credentials from the parent).","Define Licence Credentials... - use this to access the licence credentials definition area where a user can define additional configuration licence constraints to a folder:","Please see the Add a folder help topic for information on how to proceed.","Add folder dialog","Addfolderdialog.htm");
Page[63]=new Array("Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained in the Solution.  Folders are stored in the shared area and displayed in the Explorer window and can be added to a solution or to a folder.","To add a folder to a solution or a folder","In the Explorer window, right click on the solution or the folder to which you want to add the new folder.","Select Add folder.","In the Add folder dialog, type the name of the new folder in to the Name field. ","You must select the components to be allowed within this folder. ","To filter the component types according to categories, select the required categories from the drop-down list. By default, the categories is displayed as &quot;All Categories&quot;.    ","Use the buttons in the middle of the Add folder dialog to allow or prevent the use of component types in the folder:","&gt; to add selected","&gt;&gt; to add all","&lt; to remove selected","&lt;&lt; to remove all","Copy from parent: copies all component types from the parent of the selected folder.","To filter the list of components displayed, choose a category from the drop-down list","Once you have selected the required components, click on the OK button.","The system will check to ensure that this name is unique within the solution. The Add folder dialog will close. You will now be able to add components to this folder. Use Manage Allowed Component types to amend any of the selections you have made.","To configure license constraints in the folder, please see the Define additional configuration licence constraints help topic for more information.","Add a folder","Addafolder.htm");
Page[64]=new Array("Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained in the Solution. Folders are stored in the shared area and displayed in the Explorer window. ","A folder can not be deleted if it contains components which are located in the shared repository.","The removal of a folder will mean deletion of its content.","Publishing rules will also be deleted.","A user must have the Architect role to delete a folder.","To delete a folder","In the Explorer window, right click on the folder that you wish to remove.","Select Delete.","In the Confirm Object Deletion dialog box, click on the Yes button to confirm the deletion.","The folder will be deleted.","Delete a folder","Deleteafolder.htm");
Page[65]=new Array("Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained in the Solution. Folders are stored in the shared area and displayed in the Explorer window. The user can rename a folder.","To rename a folder","In the Explorer window, right click on the folder you wish to rename.","Select Rename.","In the Rename dialog, type the new name in the New name field.","Click on the OK button.","The system will check to ensure that this name is unique within the solution and rename the folder.","Rename a folder","Renameafolder.htm");
Page[66]=new Array("Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained in the solution. Folders are stored in the shared area and displayed in the Explorer window. ","Folders can be published. The publishing mechanism allows for the sharing of components between folders within the solution boundary, for example; definitions of data models and layouts can be located in a folder and published for use within other parts of the solution, but not within other solutions. ","Without the publishing capability the user would need to re-create the components in multiple folders, duplicating effort and components in order to use the definitions throughout the solution.","The publishing mechanism is activated from any folder within the Explorer window. This folder is known as the source folder and contains the components that will be published to other folders.","Folder A contains a logical data source that contains generic application characteristics, folder B will be where the scorecards are created, and folder C will be where the segmentation rules will be created. ","By publishing from the source folder (folder A) to folders B and C, the scorecards and segmentation rules can be built using the characteristics defined in folder A. ","Publishing folder B to folder C enables the segmentation rules to be used to define the scorecard. ","Any amendments made to the original component will automatically be updated to the published instances of the component throughout the solution without the need for any further action.","The publishing mechanism will only be available to those users who have the appropriate access rights. ","When Publish is selected from the Explorer window the Publishing editor is opened along with the Publishing Inventory window.","Please see the Publish directly to another folder and the Publish to parent or child folders help pages for more information on this.","Publish a folder","Publishafolder.htm");
Page[67]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The user may validate a Folder from the Explorer window.","To validate a Folder ","In the Explorer window, select the Folder that you wish to validate.","Right click and select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validate a Folder","ValidateaFolder.htm");
Page[68]=new Array("Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained within a solution. Folders are stored in the shared area and displayed in the Explorer window."," @","Orphaned components are components that no longer have a parent folder; components whose parent folder has been deleted in a multi user environment. These components are held in the Orphaned Components folder in the Explorer window.  ","@The Orphaned Components folder will only be displayed when active. ","Components from the Orphaned Components folder can be relocated into other folders or deleted if required.","In a multi user environment, 2 users are working in the same folder. Both are creating components within the same folder without checking them in. If one of the users deletes the folder, the components no longer have a parent folder and are moved into the Orphaned Components folder.","Orphaned Components folder","OrphanedComponentsfolder.htm");
Page[69]=new Array("A component is an entity within a Solution that carries out a particular business function. Examples include Decision Process Flows, Scorecards, Logical Data Source etc. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window.","Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained in the solution. Folders can contain many different types of component It makes things easier if components of a similar type are grouped together, for example; segmentation devices, decision process flows, etc. ","Components are created in the Explorer window. Before the user can create a specific component the allowed component types for each folder of a solution must be defined to enable the creation of components inside them. ","Components are first saved in the user repository. The user needs to check them in to the shared repository to make them available for other users. By doing this, an automatic component history is generated and the user has the possibility to revert components.","The user can import a previously exported component, folder or solution along with any dependent components and folder structures.","The user can export a component, folder or solution along with any dependant components and folder structures.","Component overview","Componentoverview.htm");
Page[70]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. ","Folders can contain many different types of component. It makes things easier if components of a similar type are grouped together within a solution; for example, segmentation devices, decision process flows, etc. ","A greyed out component type in the right field corresponds to a component type already in use in this folder; this component type cannot be removed unless the component(s) are deleted first.","Manage allowed component types allows the user to determine which components should be held in which folders. The user can also define additional configuration licence constraints to a folder.","This is only available to users who have Architect permissions.","To manage allowed component types","In the Explorer window, right click on the folder and select Manage allowed component types.","In the Manage allowed component types dialog, in the Categories field select the pre-defined set of components required from the drop-down list.","Use the buttons in the middle to allow or to prevent the use of components within the folder:","&gt;  -  use this to add a selected component from the left field to the allowed component types.","&gt;&gt; -  use this to add all components from the left field to the allowed component types.","&lt;  -  use this to remove a selected component from the allowed component types.","&lt;&lt; -  use this to remove all components from the allowed component types.","Copy from parent - use this to copy all component types from the parent of the selected folder.","When you have all the required component types in the allowed component types field, click on the OK button to finish.","To configure license constraints in the folder, please see the Define additional configuration licence constraints help topic for more information.","The Manage allowed component types dialog will close, and the folder will be updated.","Manage allowed component types in a folder","Manageallowedcomponenttypesinafolder.htm");
Page[71]=new Array("The Manage allowed component types dialog allows the user to determine which components should be held in which folders. ","The dialog consists of:","Categories field - the user can select a pre-defined set of components for any particular system by selecting a specific category from the drop-down list.","Left field - displays the pre-defined set of components within the selected category.","Right field: Allowed component types - displays the selected allowed component types.","&gt;  -  use this to add a selected component from the left field to the allowed component types.","&gt;&gt; -  use this to add all components from the left field to the allowed component types.","&lt;  -  use this to remove a selected component from the allowed component types.","&lt;&lt; -  use this to remove all components from the allowed component types.","Copy from parent - use this to copy all component types from the parent of the selected folder (copying from parent will also copy the licence credentials from the parent).","Define Licence Credentials... - use this to access the licence credentials definition area where a user can define additional configuration licence constraints to a folder:","Please see the Manage allowed component types help topic for information on how to proceed.","Manage allowed component types dialog","Manageallowedcomponenttypesdialog.htm");
Page[72]=new Array("By default, all allowed components (as defined in the Manage allowed components dialog) will be accessible in a folder, subject to a user's role permissions and the capability licence in use. If additional configuration licence constraints are to be applied to a folder, a user can define this in the Manage allowed components types dialog.","To define additional configuration licence constraints to a folder","In the Manage allowed component types dialog, click on the Define Licence Credentials button.","The definition area will be displayed:","Using the drop down list, select the licence level for which you wish to define constraints (Architect, Designer or Anyone).","Configure as appropriate by clicking on the appropriate component type and activity; the tick will change with each click:","When the activity column for a component type displays a @, this means that the current licence level selected (Architect, Designer, Anyone) is the minimum required to carry out this action.","When the activity column for a component type displays a @, this means that the lower licence level (a lower level than the currently selected one) has been specified as the minimum required for this activity.","When the activity column for a component type displays a  @, this means that a higher licence has been specified as the minimum required for this activity.","Click on the OK button to finish.","The licence credential constraints for the folder are now configured.","To manage the allowed components types within this folder, please see the Manage allowed component types in a folder help topic for more information.","Define licence constraints to a folder","Definelicenceconstraintstoafolder.htm");
Page[73]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. The user can add a component to a folder within the Explorer window.","Folders are used to provide an organisational structure for the components contained in the solution. Folders can contain many different types of component. It makes things easier if components of a similar type are grouped together; for example, segmentation devices, decision process flows, etc.","To add a component to a folder","In the Explorer window, right click on the folder you want to add a component to.","You will only be able to add a component type that has been allowed for the selected folder. If it is not allowed it will not be listed and therefore cannot be created. Please see the managed allowed component types help page for more information on this.","Select Add component.","In the Create component dialog, delete the default name and enter the name of the new component in the name field.","If you wish to have the new component display in the Main editor on creation, ensure that the Open new components in component editor tick box is selected.","Click on the OK button.","The system will check to ensure that this name is unique within the solution. ","If the tick box is selected, the newly created component will be displayed in the Explorer window within the selected folder. If the tick box is not selected the component will be listed in the appropriate folder.","Add a component to a folder","Addacomponenttoafolder.htm");
Page[74]=new Array("The Create component dialog enables a user to add a component to a folder.","Please see the Add a component to a folder help topic for information on how to proceed.","Create component dialog","Createcomponentdialog.htm");
Page[75]=new Array("Components can be deleted from the User domain or from the User and Shared domains.  Deleting a component from the User domain will remove the component from just the User domain; deleting a component from the Shared domain will physically remove components from the repository, enabling a user to remove components that have become redundant from the solution to 'clean' it up. ","The Delete option can be accessed from all components when a user has been given suitable security privileges. The option that they can select will be dependent on whether the component exists just in the User domain or has been checked into the repository. The two options are:","Delete a component from User domain","Delete a component from User and Shared domains","The keyboard 'Del' key can be used to delete a component when it has been selected in the Explorer. The type of delete option carried out will depend on the component location:","- When it is located in the User domain, pressing 'Del' key will delete it from the User domain<br>- When it is located in the Shared domain, pressing 'Del' key will delete it from the Shared domain<br>- When it is located in both User and Shared domains, pressing 'Del' will delete it from the User domain only","While Deleting","The system will not allow the delete function to work if:","at least an editor of the items to be deleted is open","dependencies with other components exist in the User or Shared areas","a component has an Edition label of &quot;Pending&quot;, &quot;Reject&quot; or &quot;Sanction&quot;","the component is in use by another component for which you do not have access","If any of these occur a warning message will be displayed informing the user that the item(s) cannot be deleted and the reason why and (if applicable) refer the user to the Output window for more information.","It is therefore recommended that you use the Where Used function before attempting to delete so that you can work out where dependencies exist.","To delete a component from a User domain","In the Explorer window, right click on the component that you wish to delete.","Select Delete followed by Delete from User domain.","Delete from User domain option will be available on new components and components that have been checked out. ","In the Confirm Object Deletion dialog, click on the Yes button.","The component will be deleted from the folder.","To delete a component from the User domain and Shared domain (Repository)","In the Explorer window, right click on the component that you wish to delete.","Select Delete followed by Delete from User domain and Shared domains.","Delete from User and Shared domains will be available on components that have been checked in.","In the Confirm Object Deletion dialog, click on the Yes button.","The component will be deleted from both the User domain and the Shared domains.","After a component has been deleted:","When a component has been deleted from the Shared area, all other users that have checked this component out into their own User area will be informed via the Output Window that this component has been deleted. A new copy of the deleted component will be created in their User area.","If a user tries to check-out a revision of a component that has been deleted the check-out will fail and the user will be informed of the issue in the Output Window.","If a user tries to check-out a label that uses a deleted component the check-out will fail and the user will be informed of the issue in the Output Window.","Delete a component","Deleteacomponent.htm");
Page[76]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. The user can copy a component to another folder within the Explorer window. The selected component will still exists in the source folder. ","Component dependencies are not copied. Once the copy has been completed, if there is no broken dependency, nothing needs to be done. If the component has some broken dependencies, this will be detailed in the output window. ","To copy a component using copy and paste","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to copy.","Select Copy. ","Right click on the folder where you wish to copy the component to.","Select Paste.","A copy of the component will be displayed in the folder. You can rename the component if required.","Paste will not be available if the component type is not allowed in the destination folder, or if the user does not have create permission for this destination folder.","If a component with the same name already exists in the target folder, the component is renamed to &quot;Copy of&quot;, &quot;Copy (2) of&quot;, etc. Please see the Rename a component topic for more information on renaming.","To copy a component using drag and drop","To copy a component using the drag and drop function alone, the component must be checked in. If the component is not checked in, the drag and drop function will move the selected component into a new folder, removing it from the source folder. You may copy using drag and drop along with the Ctrl button.","In the Explorer window, select and drag the component into the required folder.","A copy of the component will now be displayed in the appropriate folder. You can rename the component if required.","Drop will not be available if the component type is not allowed in the destination folder, or if the user does not have create permission for this destination folder.","If a component with the same name already exists in the target folder, the component is renamed to &quot;Copy of&quot;, &quot;Copy (2) of&quot;, etc. Please see the Rename a component topic for more information on renaming.","Copy a component","Copyacomponent.htm");
Page[77]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. The user can save and copy a component to a folder within the Explorer window.","To save and copy a component","To save and copy a component, the component must be open for editing in the Main editor.","Click on File in the Main menu bar and select Save &amp; Copy As.","The Copy Component dialog will be initiated. Type the new name for the component copy in the name field.","Click on the OK button.","The copy component will be saved and a copy of it will now be displayed in the same folder as the original component.","Save and copy a component","Saveandcopyacomponent.htm");
Page[78]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. The user can move a component to another folder within the Explorer window. ","If a component has been checked in, it can not be moved.","To move a component using drag and drop","In the Explorer window, select and drag the component into the required folder.","The component will now be displayed in the appropriate folder. ","Drop will not be available if the component type is not allowed in the destination folder, or if the user does not have create permission for this destination folder.","If a component with the same name already exists in the target folder, the user will be prompted with the error message; Name already exists. To rename the component, please see the Rename a component topic for more information on renaming.","To move a component using cut and paste","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to move.","Select Cut. ","Right click on the folder where you want to move the component to.","Select Paste.","The component will now be displayed in the appropriate folder. ","Paste will not be available if the component type is not allowed in the destination folder, or if the user does not have create permission for this destination folder.","If a component with the same name already exists in the target folder, the component is renamed to &quot;Copy of&quot;, &quot;Copy (2) of&quot;, etc. To rename the component, please see the Rename a component topic for more information on renaming.","Move a component","Moveacomponent.htm");
Page[79]=new Array("Orphaned components are components that no longer have a parent folder; components whose parent folder has been deleted in a multi user environment. These components are held in the Orphaned Components folder in the Explorer window.  ","@The Orphaned Components folder will only be displayed when active. ","Components from the Orphaned Components folder can be relocated into other folders.","To relocate an orphaned component ","In the Explorer window, select and drag the orphaned component into the required folder.","The component will now be displayed in the appropriate folder. ","This function will not be available if the component type is not allowed in the destination folder, or if the user does not have create permission for this destination folder.","If a component with the same name already exists in the target folder, the component is renamed to &quot;Copy of&quot;, &quot;Copy (2) of&quot;, etc. Please see the Rename a component topic for more information on renaming.","Component dependencies are not moved. If there is no broken dependency, nothing needs to be done. If the component has some broken dependencies, this will be detailed in the output log. ","Relocation of orphaned components","Relocationoforphanedcomponents.htm");
Page[80]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. The user can edit or configure components as required.","To edit a component","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to edit or configure.","Select Open. ","The component you have selected will open for editing in the Main editor.","Double clicking on a component will open the component in the Main editor.","Edit a component","Editacomponent.htm");
Page[81]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. ","The name of a component can be changed.","To rename a component","To rename a component, the component must be checked out. To rename a component that is checked in, you must check it out, rename it and then check it back in.","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to rename.","Select Rename.","In the Rename Component dialog,  enter the new name of the component.","Click on the OK button.","The system will check to ensure that this name is unique within the current folder. The renamed component is now displayed in the Explorer window within the selected folder. ","Rename a component","Renameacomponent.htm");
Page[82]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. A user can check in a component. Check in moves the component to the shared area which makes it available for other users.","You will be unable to check in a component whilst it is open for editing in the Main editor.","To check in a component","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to check in.","Select Check-in. The Check-in wizard will be initiated.","In the Check-in wizard, ensure that the Accept Warning check box is ticked.","Make sure that the component you want to check in is selected.","Type a comment into the Comment field. This field is mandatory.","If required, click on the@ button to choose a label from the list of existing labels in the Label Chooser dialog or start typing the label information. If you type a name, automatic suggestions will appear, select as appropriate from the drop-down box.","Click on the Next button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component name in the Explorer window changes from bold to normal characters.","The user can check the component back out if required.","To carry out this procedure on multiple components within a folder, right click on the folder and select Manage components. Select Check-in. In the initiated wizard, make sure that the required components are selected. Enter the comment and the label information (the comment field is mandatory). Click on the OK button then click on the Finish button.","Check in a component","Checkinacomponent.htm");
Page[83]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. A user can check in a component. Check in moves the component to the shared repository which makes it available for other users.","The Check-in wizard enables the user to check in a component.","Please see the Check in a component help topic for information on how to proceed.","Check-in wizard","Check-inwizard.htm");
Page[84]=new Array("The Label Chooser dialog is prompted when the user checks in a component.","The label given can be used to access the component set from the shared repository for export, check out, printing, deployment, etc. It is also used for versioning, to stamp a label onto a set of components or revisions to record the fact that they have been subjected to a specific action.","Labels can be created when updated or newly created components are checked in; the user can either create a new label or use an existing label (thus adding the component to an existing set). Labels can also be used when components are imported into a shared repository, to tag the set of components brought into the system. Finally, the user can use labeling to pull together a component set by selecting individual components from the solution explorer; by assigning a label to a group of related components at the folder or solution level; or by some automatic discovery process (for example, all components referenced by a particular process flow).","While one label can be assigned to many different components, the same label cannot be assigned to different revisions of the same component. This is because labeling is intended to keep track of the various revisions in a coherent system.","The list of all labels in the solution is displayed:","At the bottom of the dialog is a set of buttons that allows the users to narrow the display of labels; to create a new label; or to display a list of components assigned to a label:","@ All labels - display the list of all labels in the solution","@ My labels - display only the labels you created or modified","@ Recently changed - display labels that were changed in the past 7 days","@ Create label - create a new label for this component","@ Show label - display all components that are assigned the selected label","Please see the Assign a label to a component, folder or solution help topic for more information on this.","Label chooser","Labelchooser.htm");
Page[85]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. The user can check out a component. Checking out a component takes the specific revision of the component from the shared area into the user area.","To check out a component","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to check out.","Select Check-out. The Check-out wizard will be initiated.","In the Check-out wizard, make sure that the component you want to check out is selected.","Click on the Next button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component name in the Explorer window changes from normal to bold characters.","The user can check a component back in if required.","To carry out this procedure on multiple components within a folder, right click on the folder and select Manage components. Select Check-out. In the initiated wizard, make sure that the required components are selected. Click on the OK button then click on the Finish button.","Check out a component","Checkoutacomponent.htm");
Page[86]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. The user can check out a component. Checking out a component takes the specific revision of the component from the shared area into the user area.","The Check-out wizard enables the user to check out a component.","Please see the Check out a component help topic for information on how to proceed.","Check-out wizard","Check-outwizard.htm");
Page[87]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window.","Locking a component prevents other users from saving any changes made to the component back to the repository. A user can lock any component that is within the Shared area. If a component is already locked or if the user does not have appropriate update permissions, the user will be unable to lock it.","Other users can copy locked component to their workspace.They will not be able to lock the component or update any of the changes they have made to this component to the repository.","To lock a component","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to lock.","Select Lock.","In the Lock wizard, make sure that the component you want to lock is selected.","Click on the Next button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component is marked with the @ icon in the Inventory window. ","Components can be unlocked to allow other users to save changes to them back to the repository. A component can only be unlocked by the user who locked it. ","To carry out this procedure on multiple components within a folder, right click on the folder and select Manage components. Select Lock. In the initiated wizard, make sure that the required components are selected. Click on the OK button and then click on the Finish button.","Locking a component","Lockingacomponent.htm");
Page[88]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window.","Locking a component prevents other users from saving any changes made to the component back to the repository. A user can lock any component that is within the Shared Domain. If a component is already locked or if the user does not have appropriate update permissions, the user will be unable to lock it.","The Lock wizard enables a user to lock a component.","Please see the Locking a component help topic for information on how to proceed.","Lock wizard","Lockwizard.htm");
Page[89]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window.","Locking a component prevents other users from saving any changes to the component back to the repository. A user can lock any component that is within the Shared area. ","Components can be unlocked to allow other users to save changes to them back to the repository. ","A component can only be unlocked by the user who locked it or by a user with the solution administrator role.","To unlock a component","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to unlock.","Select Unlock.","In the Unlock wizard, make sure that the component you want to unlock is selected.","Click on the Next button.","Click on the Finish button.","In the Inventory window, the @ icon disappears from the row of the selected component.","To carry out this procedure on multiple components within a folder, right click on the folder and select Manage components. Select Unlock. In the initiated wizard, make sure that the required components are selected. Click on the OK button then click on the Finish button.","Unlocking a component","Unlockingacomponent.htm");
Page[90]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. Locking a component prevents other users from saving any changes to the component back to the repository. A user can lock any component that is within the Shared Domain. Components can be unlocked to allow other users to save changes to them back to the repository. ","The Unlock wizard allows a user to unlock a component.","Please see the Unlocking a component help topic for information on how to proceed.","Unlock wizard","Unlockwizard.htm");
Page[91]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window.","A component can be marked as a favourite in the Explorer window. Favourites can be viewed in one place by using the Explorer view bar, making them easier to locate. This means that the user can select components used on a regular basis as favourites. ","Mark a component as a favourite.","In the Explorer window, right click on the required component.","Select Mark as favourite.","The component will now display in your favourites folder when selected from the Explorer view bar in the Explorer window.","Mark a component as a favourite","Markacomponentasafavourite.htm");
Page[92]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. ","The user can choose to show or hide components within folders in the Explorer window. Hiding a component is an alternative to deletion, giving the user the possibility to restore it later without having to create it again. On hiding a component, the component will be given a subsequent hidden revision number. Hiding a component will not affect component validation and the component can still be referenced by other components. The user can then reinstate the component to full usability if required by choosing to show the hidden component. On showing the component, the component will be given a subsequent not hidden revision number. The revision details are stored and can be viewed in the Inventory window.","To show a hidden component","A component must be hidden. To see any hidden components, in the Explorer window and in the Explorer view bar, click on the @ icon.","Any hidden components will be displayed in red with a strikethrough.","Right click on the component that you wish to show.","Select Show.","The Show wizard will be initiated.","In the Show wizard, make sure that the component you want to show is selected.","Type a comment into the Comment field. This field is mandatory.","Click on the@ button to choose a label from the list of existing labels in the Label Chooser dialog or start typing the label information. If you type a name, automatic suggestions will appear, select as appropriate from the drop-down box.","Click on the OK button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component name will now be displayed in the Explorer window. ","Show a hidden component","Showahiddencomponent.htm");
Page[93]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. The user can choose to show or hide components within folders in the Explorer window. Hiding a component is an alternative to deletion, giving the user the possibility to restore it later without having to create it again. On hiding a component, the component will be given a subsequent hidden revision number. Hiding a component will not affect component validation and the component can still be referenced by other components. The user can then reinstate the component to full usability if required by choosing to show the hidden component. On showing the component, the component will be given a subsequent not hidden revision number. The revision details are stored and can be viewed in the Inventory window.","The Show wizard enables a user to show a component.","Please see the Show a component help topic for information on how to proceed.","Show wizard","Showwizard.htm");
Page[94]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. ","The user can choose to show or hide components within folders in the Explorer window. Hiding a component is an alternative to deletion, giving the user the possibility to restore it at a later date without having to create it again. On hiding a component, the component will be given a subsequent hidden revision number. Hiding a component will not affect component validation and the component can still be referenced by other components. The revision details are stored and can be viewed in the Inventory window. The user can recreate the component to full usability, please see the show a component procedure topic for more information.","To hide a component","A component must be checked in if you wish to hide it.","In the Explorer window, right click on the component that you wish to hide.","Select Hide.","The Hide wizard will be initiated.","In the Hide wizard, make sure that the component you want to hide is selected.","Type a comment into the Comment field. This field is mandatory.","Click on the@ button to choose a label from the list of existing labels in the Label Chooser dialog or start typing the label information. If you type a name, automatic suggestions will appear, select as appropriate from the drop-down box.","Click on the OK button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component name will no longer be displayed in the Explorer window. ","The Show/Hide Obsolete icon in the Explorer view bar can be used to show or hide hidden components in the Explorer window.","Hide a component","Hideacomponent.htm");
Page[95]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. The user can choose to show or hide components within folders in the Explorer window. Hiding a component is an alternative to deletion, giving the user the possibility to restore it at a later date without having to create it again. Hiding a component will not affect component validation and the component can still be referenced by other components.","The Hide wizard enables the user to hide a component.","Please see the Hide a component help topic for information on how to proceed.","Hide wizard","Hidewizard.htm");
Page[96]=new Array("Labels can be unassigned to components from the Label Inventory.","An Edition label cannot be unassigned.","To unassign a label","Open the Label Inventory from the Label Management editor or from the Label Chooser screen of any of the label wizards, by selecting a label and clicking the View components button @.","Click on the component for which you want to unassign the label, or select multiple labels by holding down the Ctrl key while selecting the labels, then right click on a label and select Unassign label from the menu.","At the prompt, click Yes to unassign the component(s).","The label(s) has been usassigned from the component(s).","Unassign a label to a component","Unassignalabeltoacomponent.htm");
Page[97]=new Array("Component history is used to trace the previous versions of a component. Every time a component is checked in, a new version of it is created. Every time a component is checked in, a version is saved in the history of that component; meaning that any pre-existing versions are already there in the shared domain and when you check in an updated component from the user domain a new version / revision is added. Each saved version is given a revision number and can be viewed in the History window. ","The user has the ability to revert back to an earlier version if required. Carrying out this process will replace the user area version with a copy of the specific revision from the shared area.","Only components that are checked out can be reverted, please see Check out a component.","To revert a component to a previous version","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to revert.","Select History.","The History window will be initiated. Please see the History window help page for more information on this window.","Right click anywhere in the Revision row that you wish to revert to.","Select Revert to this revision.","The Revert to this revision wizard will be initiated.","Ensure that the version you would like to revert to is selected.","Click on the Next button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component versions in both the shared and user area can be seen in the Component Revisions section in the Properties window.","Revert a component to a previous version","Revertacomponenttoapreviousversion.htm");
Page[98]=new Array("Component history is used to trace the previous versions of a component. Every time a component is checked in, a new version of it is created. The user has the ability to revert back to an earlier version if required.","The Revert to this revision wizard enables the user to revert back to an earlier revision.","Please see the Revert a component to a previous version help topic for information on how to proceed.","Revert to this revision wizard","Reverttothisrevisionwizard.htm");
Page[99]=new Array("Component history is used to trace the previous versions of a component. Every time a component is checked in, a new version of it is created. The user has the ability to revert to the last revision from the Shared Area.","Only components that are checked out can be reverted, please see Check out a component.","To revert a component to latest revision from shared area","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you wish to revert.","Select Revert.","The Revert wizard will be initiated.","Ensure that the version you want to revert to is listed and selected.","Click on the Next button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component versions in both the shared and user area can be seen in the Component Revisions section in the Properties window.","Revert a component to latest revision from shared area","Revertacomponenttolatestrevisionfromsharedarea.htm");
Page[100]=new Array("Component history is used to trace the previous versions of a component. Every time a component is checked in, a new version of it is created. The user has the ability to revert to the last revision from the Shared Area.","The Revert wizard enables a user to revert to the last revision in the shared area.","Please see the Revert a component to latest version from shared area help topic for information on how to proceed.","Revert wizard","Revertwizard.htm");
Page[101]=new Array("Component history is used to trace the previous versions of a component. Every time a component is checked in, a new version of it is created.","To display component history","In the Explorer window, right click on the component for which you want to view the history.","Select History.","The History window is displayed. For more detail on the History window, please see the History window help page.","Display component history","Displaycomponenthistory.htm");
Page[102]=new Array("A component is an entity within a solution that carries out a particular business function. Components are stored and displayed in the Explorer window. The user can view the properties for a component.","To view component properties","In the Explorer window, right-click on the component you want to view the properties for.","Select Properties.","The Properties window will be initiated.","View component properties","Viewcomponentproperties.htm");
Page[103]=new Array("Components can be tested to assess their effectiveness prior to operational implementation. ","Please see the Interactive Tester and Batch Tester help topics for more information.","Testing components","Testingcomponents.htm");
Page[104]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","Validating a component automatically validates any referenced or embedded components.","The user may validate a Component from the Main Menu or the Main tool bar. On doing this, any changes made to the component in an open editor that have not yet been saved will be taken into account during validation. ","To validate a component from the Main Menu","You must have the component you wish to validate open in the Main editor and in focus.","From the Main menu bar, click on File.","From the drop-down list select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","To validate a component from the Main tool bar","You must have the component you wish to validate open in the Main editor and in focus.","From the Main tool bar, click on @ icon.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","The user may validate a component in the Explorer window. On doing this, any changes made to the component in an open editor will not be taken into account and the validation will be performed on the user/shared area component. ","To validate a component from the Explorer window","In the Explorer window, select the Component that you wish to validate.","Right click and select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validate a Component","ValidateaComponent.htm");
Page[105]=new Array("The user can select an individual component from the Explorer and assign a label to it; or the user can assign a label to all or some of the components within a selected folder or solution. ","The assigned label can be created as part of this process, or it can be a pre-existing label that may or may not include other components. The selected component can be added to the label by itself, or along with some or all of its dependent components. These various options are all managed by the Assign label wizard.  ","A label can also be assigned whenever a check-in action is performed on a component.","To assign a label to a component","From the Explorer window right click on a component and choose Assign label. The first screen of the Assign label wizard, Component Chooser, is displayed:","Select whether to; include only a custom selection of dependencies with the component by checking the tickbox or leave the tickbox unchecked to include all dependent components in the label. (The Select All and Unselect All buttons are not relevant in this set of instructions, as only one component has been selected for assignment.)","If more than one revision of this component exists, you can select the revision number to which you want to apply the label from the drop down list in the Revision column.","Continue at step 4 below.","To assign a label to a folder or solution","From the Explorer window right click on a folder or a solution and choose Manage components, then select Assign label. The first screen of the Assign label wizard, Component Chooser, is displayed:","Select whether to; include only a custom selection of dependencies with the component by checking the tickbox or leave the tickbox unchecked to include all dependent components in the label.","If more than one revision of any component exists, you can select the revision number to which you want to apply the label from the drop down list in the Revision column.","Click on the Next button. If the Custom selection tickbox has been left unchecked, the wizard skips to the third screen. If the tickbox has been checked, clicking on the Next button displays the second screen of the wizard, Custom selection of dependencies:","By default, all dependent components are selected to be included in the label along with the original component(s). Unselect the components you do not want to include in the label, or click on the @ button to include none of the dependent components. Click on  the @ button to display the Revision information.  ","Click on the Next button to display the third screen of the wizard, Label Chooser. A list of all labels in the solution is displayed:","At the bottom of the screen is a set of buttons that allow you to limit the display of labels to those that you have created, to display labels created recently, to create a new label or to display a list of components assigned to a label:","@ All labels - display the list of all labels in the solution","@ My labels - display only the labels you have created or modified","@ Recently changed - display labels that were changed in the past 7 days","@ Create label - create a new label for this component","@ Show label - display all components that are assigned the selected label: ","Select a label to assign or create a new label for the component(s).","It is not possible to select multiple labels.","Click on the Next button to display the fourth screen of the wizard; Summary. This displays information about the label you are creating and the list of components to which you are assigning the label. If the information displayed is correct, click on the Finish button to create the label.","The label has now been assigned to the selected component, folder or solution.","Assign a label to a component, folder or solution","Assignalabeltoacomponent,folderorsolution.htm");
Page[106]=new Array("The Server Connections Manager enables the user to view the server connections to servers that host the following:","Solution repositories","Content repositories","Reporting repositories","Job servers","The Server Connections Manager is relative to the Experian Decision Analytics security&nbsp;server configuration which is not editable in this view. This window displays the kind of connections available and identifies if &nbsp;the current configuration is connected to the correct content/solution repositories.","The configuration is defined by the Experian Decision Analytics security server administrators and can not be viewed&nbsp;by a normal user (except with this view). ","All remote connections viewed here are relative to the Experian Decision Analytics servers. ","The Server Connections Manager window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software the Server Connections Manager window will not be displayed. It can be initiated from the Main menu bar. Once initiated, it will display on the left hand side of the interface.","Server Connections Manager overview","ServerConnectionsManageroverview.htm");
Page[107]=new Array("The Server Connections Manager window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software the Server Connections Manager window will not be displayed. It can be initiated from the Main menu bar. Once initiated, it will display on the left hand side of the interface.","The Server Connections Manager is a read only window.","The Server Connections Manager window allows the user to view the server connections to servers that host the following:","@ Solution Repositories - A Solution Repository is used to hold a secure and persisted copy of the client&#8217;s system(s) which can be accessed and updated by the users of the Studio applications. These users may be collaborating on changes to shared systems or may be working alongside each other in separate areas of a system (or on separate systems); the Repository provides an archive and audit trail of changes made by these users during the lifetime of the systems.","@ Content Repositories - A Content Repository is used to hold template content. This template content can then be used as a basis to facilitate the rapid construction of strategies.","@ Reporting Repositories - Reporting Repositories contain report output objects. These output objects hold the latest results from reports configured in the Solution Repositories.","@ Job servers - This displays connections to servers on which the Job Submission functionality can run. The job server role is to execute asynchronous actions which&nbsp;can be time consuming, such as batch process flow. import/export and deployment.","Server Connections Manager window","ServerConnectionsManagerwindow.htm");
Page[108]=new Array("If the Server Connections Manager window is not visible in the user interface, the user can initiate this at any time.","To initiate the Server Connections Manager window","In the main system view, click on the Window option in the Main menu bar and select Server Connections Manager.","The Server Connections Manager window will now display in its predefined location in the user interface.","You can drag and drop the Server Connections Manager window to any preferred location. Please see the Customise the User Interface help page for more information on this.","Initiate the Server Connections Manager window","InitiatetheServerConnectionsManagerwindow.htm");
Page[109]=new Array("The Navigator displays the contents of a selected component and its dependencies.","The Navigator window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default the Navigator window is displayed on the left hand side of the interface beneath the Explorer window.","The Navigator window is populated when the user left clicks on a component in the Explorer window or when the user opens a component in the Main editor. ","Navigator overview","Navigatoroverview.htm");
Page[110]=new Array("The Navigator window is housed in the Explorer area of the User Interface. By default on opening the software the Navigator window will be displayed on the left hand side of the interface beneath the Explorer window.","If the Navigator window has been closed, it can be reopened at any time. Please see the Initiate the Navigator window help page for further information.","The Navigator window displays the contents of a selected component and its dependencies.","The Navigator window is populated when the user left clicks on a component in the Explorer window or when the user opens a component in the Main editor. ","The user can perform some actions by right clicking on a component in the Navigator window. The actions available depend upon the component. Available actions are the same as the actions available in the Explorer window; please see the Explorer window help page for further information.","Navigator window","Navigatorwindow.htm");
Page[111]=new Array("The Navigator window displays the contents of a selected component and its dependencies.","If the Navigator window is not visible in the User Interface, it can be initiated from the Main menu bar.","To initiate the Navigator window","In the main system view, click on the Window option in the Main menu bar and select Navigating.","Select Navigator.","The Navigator window will be initiated at the bottom left hand side of the User Interface.","The Navigator window is populated when the user left clicks on a component in the Explorer window or when the user opens a component in the Main editor.","Initiate the Navigator window","InitiatetheNavigatorwindow.htm");
Page[112]=new Array("The Satellite View is the area of the user interface where the the user can view a reduced image of the Main editor. If the process in the Main editor is too large to view in full the reduced image enables the user to see a process fully.","The Satellite View window is initiated when the Decision Process Flow or Decision Setter components are open in the Main editor. It is also initiated when the user is publishing. ","The Satellite View window is housed in the Explorer area of the user interface. By default on opening the software the Satellite View window will be displayed on the left hand side of the interface beneath the Explorer window.","Satellite View overview","SatelliteViewoverview.htm");
Page[113]=new Array("The Satellite View is the area of the user interface where the the user can view a reduced image of the Main editor. If the process in the Main editor is too large to view in full the reduced image enables the user to see a process fully.","The Satellite View window is initiated when the Decision Process Flow or Decision Setter components are open in the Main editor. It is also initiated when the user is publishing. ","The following is an example of the Satellite View window:","The Satellite View window shows the process in the Main editor in full. The image within the grey frame in the Satellite View window represents the current view in the Main editor. The frame can be moved either by dragging and dropping or by clicking in an area within the Satellite View window, giving the user the ability to change what is viewed in the Main editor.","Satellite View window","SatelliteViewwindow.htm");
Page[114]=new Array("Where Used displays all components that have references to a selected component or characteristic.","In large solutions with multiple users modifying content, a Where Used query can be used to carry out impact analysis to assess which components are referencing (and so may be affected by changes to) a given component, enabling the user to access them and synchronise changes. ","Embedded components will not be displayed in the Where Used window.","The Where Used window when activated displays in the Explorer area of the user interface. ","Where Used can be actioned on a component from the Explorer window or on a characteristic from within a Logical Data Model or Logical Data Source. It can also be carried out from within the Where Used window.","Where Used overview","WhereUsedoverview.htm");
Page[115]=new Array("Where Used displays all components that have references to a selected component or characteristic.","In large solutions with multiple users modifying content, a Where Used query can be used to carry out impact analysis to assess which components are referencing (and so may be affected by changes to) a given component, enabling the user to access them and synchronise changes.","Embedded components will not be displayed in the Where Used window.","The Where Used window when activated displays in the Explorer area of the user interface. ","The user can activate Where Used on a component from the Explorer window or on a characteristic from within a Logical Data Model or a Logical Data Source. It can also be carried out from within the Where Used window.","The Where Used window lists any referenced component by component name in alphabetical order. ","The user can use the @button to expand all and view components that are further referenced or the @button to collapse all components. ","The user can view the referenced component in the Main editor by double clicking on the component in the Where Used window.","Where Used window","WhereUsedwindow.htm");
Page[116]=new Array("Where Used displays all components that have references to a selected component or characteristic.","In large solutions with multiple users modifying content, a Where Used query can be used to carry out impact analysis to assess which components are referencing (and so may be affected by changes to) a given component, enabling the user to access them and synchronise changes.","The Where Used window when activated displays in the Explorer area of the user interface. ","Where Used can be actioned on a component from the Explorer window or on a characteristic from within a Logical Data Model or Logical Data Source. It can also be carried out from within the Where Used window.","To view where a component is referenced","Embedded components will not be displayed in the Where Used window.","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to see the referenced components for.","Select Where Used.","The Where Used window will be initiated. All referenced components will be displayed.","To view any of the listed components in detail in the Main editor, double click on the component name or right click on the component name and select Open in the Where Used window. The component will be displayed in the Main editor area of the user interface.","You can right click on any component in the Where Used window to see any further referenced components.","For example, querying Where Used &quot;Results GenL&quot;, we get this list of multiple components that can be impacted:","Use the @button to expand all and view components that are further referenced or the @button to collapse all components. ","View where a component is referenced","Viewwhereacomponentisreferenced.htm");
Page[117]=new Array("Where Used displays all components that have references to a selected component or characteristic.","In large solutions with multiple users modifying content, a Where Used query can be used to carry out impact analysis to assess which components are referencing (and so may be affected by changes to) a given component, enabling the user to access them and synchronise changes.","The Where Used window when activated displays in the Explorer area of the user interface. ","Where Used can be actioned on a component from the Explorer window or on a characteristic from within a Logical Data Model or Logical Data Source. It can also be carried out from within the Where Used window.","To view where a characteristic is referenced","Embedded components will not be displayed in the Where Used window.","The results returned will be for the selected characteristic only and not the entire Logical Data Model or Logical Data Source.","With a Logical Data Model or Logical Data Source open in the Main editor, right click on the characteristic you want to see the referenced components for.","Select Where Used.","The Where Used window will be initiated, the system will be scanned for references and a progress bar will be displayed.","To view any of the listed components in detail in the Main editor, double click on the component name or right click on the component name and select Open in the Where Used window. The component will be displayed in the Main editor area of the user interface.","You can right click on any component in the Where Used window to see any further referenced components.","For example, querying Where Used on the characteristic &quot;Purpose of Loan&quot; in this Logical Data Source:","We get this list of multiple components that can be impacted:","Use the @button to expand all and view components that are further referenced or the @button to collapse all components. ","View where a characteristic is referenced","Viewwhereacharacteristicisreferenced.htm");
Page[118]=new Array("By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the User Interface.","The Output area houses the following windows:","The History window. ","The Inventory window. ","The Output window. ","The Publishing Inventory window. ","The Validation window.","The Search Results window.","By default on opening the software the Output area is empty. ","The History window will only be displayed when initiated from the contextual menu against a component in the Explorer window or from the Main menu bar. Please see the Initiate the History window help topic for more information.","The Inventory window will be displayed when there is an Inventory available for the folder being worked in or when initiated from the Main menu bar. ","The Output window will be displayed when the user is testing, validating or scripting or if initiated from the Main menu bar.","The Publishing Inventory window will be displayed when the user selects to Publish from a folder.","The Validation window will be displayed when the user selects to validate a Solution, Folder or Component. The Validation window will also be displayed when changes are made to a component and the changes are saved.","The Search Results window will be displayed when the user carries out an Advanced Search.","Output area","Outputarea.htm");
Page[119]=new Array("Every time a component is checked in, a version is saved in the history of that component; meaning that any pre-existing versions are already there in the shared domain and when you check in an updated component from the user domain a new version / revision is added. Each saved version of the component is given a revision number and can be viewed in the History window. ","The History of checked in components is available to the user at all times and can be viewed in the History window.","The user has the ability to revert a component to a previous version in the History window.","History overview","Historyoverview.htm");
Page[120]=new Array("The History of checked in components is available to the user at all times. ","Every time a component is checked in, a version is saved in the history of that component; meaning that any pre-existing versions are already there in the shared domain and when you check in an updated component from the user domain a new version / revision is added. Each saved version of the component is given a revision number and can be viewed in the History window. ","The History window is not displayed by default and can be initiated from the Main menu bar and from the Explorer window. Please see the Initiate the History window help page for more information on this. If the History window is closed, it can be reopened again at any time and will display in the Output area of the user interface.","When the History window is initiated for the first time in a current session, it is housed in the Output area of the User Interface. ","The History Window displays the revision number of the saved version of a component, the Date that the version was checked in, the Author at check in, the Comment at check in and the Label at check in, along with any other labels to which this revision has subsequently been added. The History window also has two columns, From and To, giving the user the option to carry out a comparison. Please see the  Comparison overview topic for more information.","The user can have more than one component open in the History window. The History window can be customised, the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view. The user can also compare versions.","The user has the ability to revert a component to a previous version in the History window.","History window","Historywindow.htm");
Page[121]=new Array("The History of checked in components is available to the user at all times. ","Every time a component is checked in, a version is saved in the history of that component; meaning that any pre-existing versions are already there in the shared domain and when you check in an updated component from the user domain a new version / revision is added. Each saved version of the component is given a revision number and can be viewed in the History window. ","The History window is not displayed by default and can be initiated from the Explorer window and from the Main menu bar.","To initiate the History window from the Explorer window","In the Explorer window, right click on the component for which you want to view the history.","Select History.","The History window is displayed.","To Initiate the History window from the Main menu bar","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select History.","The History window is displayed.","In the Explorer window, right-click on the component for which you want to view the history.","Select History.","The History window will be populated with any history data.","When the History window is initiated for the first time it is housed in the Output area of the User Interface. By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the interface.","If the History window is closed, it can be reopened again at any time, but it will display in the Main editor. The user can view it in the Main editor or move it back into the Output area by dragging and dropping the window. Please see the customize the User Interface view options help pages for more information on this. ","Initiate the History window","InitiatetheHistorywindow.htm");
Page[122]=new Array("The History window displays the revision number of the saved version of the component, the date that the version was checked in, the author at check in, the comment at check in and the label at check in. ","The History window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns in the History window.","To change the row order in the History window","In the History window, click on the header of the column by which you want to change the row order.","Data is ordered in alphabetical order starting at the top. ","To reverse the order, click again on the column header.","Change the row order in the History window","ChangetheroworderintheHistorywindow.htm");
Page[123]=new Array("The History window displays the revision number of the saved version of the component, the date that the version was checked in, the author at check in, the comment at check in and the label at check in. ","The History window can be customized; the user can change the row order, the column order and remove or add columns in the History window.","To change the column order in the History window","In the History window, drag and drop the required column header to the required column using your mouse.","The column order will now be changed.","Change the column order in the History window","ChangethecolumnorderintheHistorywindow.htm");
Page[124]=new Array("The History window displays the revision number of the saved version of the component, the date that the version was checked in, the author at check in, the comment at check in and the label at check in. ","The History window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns in the History window.","To remove or add columns in the History window","In the History window, right click on the list header.","In the Change Visible Columns dialog, tick the boxes to remove or add columns from view. Only the columns ticked will display in the History window.<br>@","Click on the OK button.","The columns ticked will display in the History window.","Remove or add columns in the History window","RemoveoraddcolumnsintheHistorywindow.htm");
Page[125]=new Array("Component history is used to trace the previous versions of a component. Every time a component is checked in, a new version of it is created. Every time a component is checked in, a version is saved in the history of that component; meaning that any pre-existing versions are already there in the shared domain and when you check in an updated component from the user domain a new version / revision is added. Each saved version is given a revision number and can be viewed in the History window. ","The user has the ability to revert back to an earlier version if required. Carrying out this process will replace the user area version with a copy of the specific revision from the shared area.","Only components that are checked out can be reverted, please see Check out a component.","To revert a component to a previous version","In the Explorer window, right click on the component you want to revert.","Select History.","The History window will be initiated. Please see the History window help page for more information on this window.","Right click anywhere in the Revision row that you wish to revert to.","Select Revert to this revision.","The Revert to this revision wizard will be initiated.","Ensure that the version you would like to revert to is selected.","Click on the Next button.","Click on the Finish button.","The component versions in both the shared and user area can be seen in the Component Revisions section in the Properties window.","Revert a component to a previous version","Revertacomponenttoapreviousversion_1.htm");
Page[126]=new Array("Every time a component is checked in, a version is saved in the history of that component; meaning that any pre-existing versions are already there in the shared domain. When you check in an updated component from the user domain a new version / revision is added. Each saved version of the component is given a revision number and can be viewed in the History window. ","The History of checked in components is available to the user at all times. A user can compare versions from the History window.","Comparison overview","Comparisonoverview.htm");
Page[127]=new Array("Every time a component is checked in, a version is saved in the history of that component; meaning that any pre-existing versions are already there in the shared domain. When you check in an updated component from the user domain a new version / revision is added. Each saved version of the component is given a revision number and can be viewed in the History window. ","The History of checked in components is available to the user at all times. A user can compare versions from the History window. Please see the Compare component versions help topic for more information.","When initiated from the History window, the Comparison editor is displayed in the main editor area of the user interface and allows the user to compare component versions:","The Comparison editor consists of a tool bar and a main area displaying the component details from the components selected by the user in the From and the To columns in the History window.","The Comparison tool bar allows the user to define what is displayed in the main area of the editor. The user can choose to show one version or both: ","@ Display only the 'From' version","@ Display only the 'To' version","@ Display both versions","The Comparison editor main area will display both the From and To versions selected by the user in the History window by default.","The main area of the Comparison editor consists of a tool bar and a read only display area. ","The main area tool bar allows the user to customise the view in the display area.","@  Save - Saves the output document on the hard drive","@  Print - Prints a hard copy of the output document","@  First Page - Navigates to the first page","@  Previous Page - Navigates to the previous page","@  Next Page - Navigates to the next page","@   Last Page - Navigates to the last page","@  Go to page - Navigates to a chosen page number","@   Actual Size - Zooms the document to its actual size","@   Fit Page - Zooms the document to fit in the preview area","@  Fit Width - Zooms the document to fit the width of the preview area","@   Zoom In - Zooms in the document to the next incremental value (e.g. 50%, 75%, etc.)","@   Zoom Out - Zooms out the document to the next incremental value (e.g. 50%, 75%, etc.)","@   Zoom Ratio - drop down list allows the user to choose a specific size of the preview","The display area is read only.","At the bottom of the Comparison editor there is information regarding the component revision being displayed and the Area in which the component sits.","Comparison editor","Comparisoneditor.htm");
Page[128]=new Array("The History of checked in components is available to the user at all times. A user can compare versions from the History window.","To compare component versions","In the Explorer window, right click on the component that you wish to compare versions.","Select History.","The History window will be initiated.","Using the radio buttons in the From and To columns in the History window, select the component versions you wish to compare;","Click on the @ icon in the History window.","The Comparison editor will initiate in the main editor area of the user interface.","Compare component versions","Comparecomponentversions.htm");
Page[129]=new Array("The Inventory of saved components is available to the user at all times. ","The Inventory window displays all components saved on the user and the shared domain, for the current folder selected by the user in the Explorer window. When a component is updated, it is automatically updated in the Inventory window.","The Inventory window is not displayed by default and can be initiated from the Main menu bar. Please see the Initiate the Inventory window help page for more information on this. ","When the Inventory window is initiated for the first time in a current session, it is housed in the Output area of the User Interface. By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the interface.","Inventory overview","Inventoryoverview.htm");
Page[130]=new Array("The Inventory of saved components is available to the user at all times. An Inventory of all components within the selected folder is given in the Inventory window.","When the Inventory window is initiated for the first time in a current session, it is housed in the Output area of the User Interface. By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the interface. If the Inventory is not displayed, it can be initiated at any time.","The user can customise this window; you can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view. ","The user can perform some actions by right clicking on a component row in the Inventory window. The actions available depend upon the component type. Available actions are the same as the actions available in the Explorer window; please see the Explorer window help page for further information.","The following options are available in the Inventory window:","@ Filter: Use this button to display or remove the Filter bar at the bottom of the Inventory window. The user can use the filter field to filter for specific component names.","@ Sub folders: Use this button to show or hide the content of sub folders.","@ Change visible columns: Use this button to choose which column you would like to view. You can also right click in the column header to initiate the Change visible columns dialog.","The following columns are available:","Component: This column displays the Component name.  ","Type: This column displays the Component Type (Decision Process Flow, Call Interface Manager, etc.)","@ Lock status: This column displays the Lock/Unlock status of the component. @  indicates that the component is locked. If the field is empty, the component is not locked. ","@ Area state: This column displays the domain that the component sits in.  @ indicates that the component sits in a user domain.  @ indicates that the component sits in a shared domain.","@ Component state: This column displays the component state.  @ indicates a new component.  @ indicates a modified component. If the field is empty, the component is unmodified.        ","@ Conflict state: This column displays the conflict state of the component. @ indicates that there is a conflict. If the field is empty, there is no conflict.","@ Broken state: This column displays the broken state of a component. @ indicates that there are no publishing rules defined between the component and a dependant component. If the field is empty, the component is not broken.","@ Favourite state: This column displays any components that the user has marked as a favourite. A user can click in here to mark a component as a favourite or to remove the favourite state.","Locked by: This column displays the user name of the user currently locking the component.","@ Revision shared area: This column displays the version number of the component on the shared domain.","@ Revision user area: This column displays the version number of the component on the user domain.","Update date: This column displays the last date that the component was updated.","Author: This column displays the author/creator of the component.","Creation date: This column displays the date the Component was created.","Name: This column displays the Name that has been given to the component.","Path: This column allows you to display the full path of a component.","Update Author: This column displays the author responsible for the latest update of the component.","Any hidden components will not display in the Inventory window. To display hidden components in the Inventory window the user must click on the Show/hide obsolete icon in the Explorer view bar. Any hidden components will then be displayed in red with a strikethrough in the Inventory window.","The text used in the Inventory window varies, please see the following descriptions:","Normal text - Item is located in the Shared Area only","Blue text - Item is located in the User Area and also in the Shared Area","Green text - Item is located in the User Area only","Red text - Item is located both in user and shared area but with an active hide flag  ","The user can customise the text colouring if required. Please see the Customise the text colouring help topic for further information on this.","Inventory window","Inventorywindow.htm");
Page[131]=new Array("The Inventory of saved components is available to the user at all times. ","The Inventory window displays all components saved on the user and the shared domain, for the current folder selected by the user in the Explorer window. When a component is updated, it is automatically updated in the Inventory window.","The Inventory window is not displayed by default and can be initiated from the Main menu bar or from the Explorer window.","To initiate the Inventory window from the Main menu bar","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select Inventory.","The Inventory window is displayed.","In the Explorer window, click on the folder for which you want to view the component Inventory.","The Inventory window will be populated with any inventory data.","When the Inventory window is initiated for the first time it is housed in the Output area of the User Interface. By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the interface.","If the Inventory window is closed, it can be reopened again at any time, but it will display in the Main editor. The user can view it in the Main editor or move it back into the Output area by dragging and dropping the window. Please see the customize the User Interface view help page for more information on this. ","Initiate the Inventory window from the Main menu bar","InitiatetheInventorywindowfromtheMainmenubar.htm");
Page[132]=new Array("Each time a user updates a component a record of the update is stored in the Inventory. This record is held and can be viewed in the Inventory window. The Inventory window will display all components within the selected folder.","The user can use the Filter text field to filter for specific component names. ","To filter component names in the Inventory window","In the Inventory window, click on the @ button.","The Filter field will now display at the bottom of the Inventory window.","Type the word you want to filter for in the free text Filter field.","The items matching the typed letters are instantly listed.","To clear the field, click on the Clear button.","To remove the Filter field from the Inventory window, click on the @ button.","The Filter text field is not case sensitive.","Filter component names in the Inventory window","FiltercomponentnamesintheInventorywindow.htm");
Page[133]=new Array("Each time a user updates a component a record of the update is stored in the Inventory. This record is held and can be viewed in the Inventory window.","The Inventory window can be customized; the user can change  the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view.","To change the row order in the Inventory window","In the Inventory window, click on the header of the column you wish to reorder.","Data is ordered in alphabetical order starting at the top. ","To reverse the order, click again on the column header.","Change the row order in the Inventory window","ChangetheroworderintheInventorywindow.htm");
Page[134]=new Array("Each time a user updates a component a record of the update is stored in the Inventory. This record is held and can be viewed in the Inventory window.","The Inventory window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view.","To change the column order in the Inventory window","In the Inventory window, drag and drop the required column header to the required column using your mouse.","The column order will be changed.","Change the column order in the Inventory window","ChangethecolumnorderintheInventorywindow.htm");
Page[135]=new Array("Each time a user updates a component a record of the update is stored in the Inventory. This record is held and can be viewed in the Inventory window.","The Inventory window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view.","To remove or add columns in the Inventory window","In the Inventory window, click on the @ button. The @ button is only visible when the scroll bar on the right of the Inventory window is visible. If not shown, make the window smaller by dragging the top of the frame toward the bottom of the screen or right click on a column header.","In the Change Visible Columns dialog, tick the boxes to remove or add columns from view. Only the columns ticked will display in the Inventory window.<br>@","Click on the OK button.","The columns ticked will display in the Inventory window.","Remove or add columns in the Inventory window","RemoveoraddcolumnsintheInventorywindow.htm");
Page[136]=new Array("To display the content of sub-folders","In the Explorer window, click on a folder.","Switch to the Inventory window.","The components in the folder you selected are displayed.","Click on the@  icon next to the component list.","The components in the sub folders of the original folder are also displayed.","When you navigate away and back to this folder, the view is reset to normal state, which means that the content of the sub-folders are not displayed.","Display sub folder content in the Inventory window","DisplaysubfoldercontentintheInventorywindow.htm");
Page[137]=new Array("Each time the user carries out testing, validation and scripting, output is generated. Output advises the user of activity, confirmation of actions, any errors, the severity of the errors, how many errors there are and in which object the errors occur.  ","Output is displayed in the Output window.","Output overview","Outputoverview.htm");
Page[138]=new Array("Each time the user carries out testing, validation and scripting, output is generated. ","The Output window displays the date and time of the output; advises the user of activity; confirms actions; notifies of any errors and the severity of the errors; displays how many errors there are and in which object the errors occur. The bottom line in the Output window advises if the test, validation or scripting is valid or invalid. ","Output is displayed in the Output window and is read only.","The Output window is not displayed by default and is initiated when the user carries out testing, validation and scripting or from the Main menu bar. Please see the Initiate the Output window help page for more information on this.","When the Output window is initiated it is housed in the Output area of the User Interface. By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the interface.","Output window","Outputwindow.htm");
Page[139]=new Array("Each time the user carries out testing, validation and scripting, output is generated. Output is displayed in the Output window. ","The Output window is not displayed by default and is initiated automatically when the user carries out testing, validation and scripting or from the Main menu bar. ","To initiate the Output window from the Main menu bar","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select Output.","From the drop-down list select Output.","The Output window will be populated with any error data.","When the Output window is initiated it is housed in the Output area of the user interface. By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the interface.","If the Output window is closed, it can be reopened again at any time.","Initiate the Output window","InitiatetheOutputwindow.htm");
Page[140]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The validation service will call an individual Solution, Folder or Component's validation service if one is registered against it. The service will then call the publishing/references service, which will check to make sure that there are no broken references or missing publishing rules within.","Validation can be done in many ways;","From the Main menu ","From the Main tool bar","In the Explorer window","The user may validate a component from the Main menu and from the Main tool bar.<br>The @ icon in the main tool bar enables the contents of an open editor to be validated."," Validation on a Solution or a Folder must be carried out from the Explorer window.","The validation service prevents the runtime object from being created from the business object if the business object is invalid. Component warnings and errors are displayed in the Validation window. By default, the Validation window is displayed in the Output area of the User Interface.","Validation overview","Validationoverview.htm");
Page[141]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The validation service prevents the runtime object from being created from the business object if the business object is invalid. Component warnings and errors are displayed in the Validation window.   ","The Validation window consists of a table containing six columns:","Level - displays the level of the validation issue:"," @ Warning - this is used when there is a possible flaw in the component that will not affect the behaviour at runtime. For example a user has specified decimal places in a class set based on an Integer characteristic."," @ Error -  this is used when a flaw in the component would prevent a runtime object from being created or the runtime component would generate invalid or misleading results. An example of misleading results would be duplicate outcome names in a class set. A user can double click on an error in the Validation window and the component will open in the main editor.","Component - displays the name of the component with the validation issue.","Type - displays the type of component with the validation issue.","Area - displays the area that the component is held in.  @ Indicates that the component is held in a user domain.  @ Indicates that the component is held in a shared domain. @ Indicates that the component is held in the active editor (or was validated from the active editor). @ Indicates that the component is embedded. A user can double click on an embedded component in the Validation window and the embedded component will open in the main editor.","Revision - displays the version number of the component.","Description - displays a description of the warning or the error.","The Validation window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view.","The Validation window also has the following:","@  Change Visible Columns - the user can click on the icon to remove or add columns in the Validation window. The Level column is mandatory. The Component, Type and Description columns are optional."," @  Validation process status bar - displays the status of the Validation process. Multiple validation tasks can be performed simultaneously if required. Running validation tasks can be viewed and cancelled.","The Validation window is not displayed by default and is initiated when the user carries out validation. Please see the Validation overview help topic for more information on this.","When the Validation window is initiated it is housed in the Output area of the User Interface. By default, the Output area is displayed at the bottom right hand side of the interface.","Validation window","Validationwindow.htm");
Page[142]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The validation service prevents the runtime object from being created from the business object if the business object is invalid. Component warnings and errors are displayed in the Validation window.","The Validation window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view.","To change the row order in the Validation window","In the Validation window, click on the header of the column you wish to reorder.","Data is ordered in alphabetical order starting at the top. ","To reverse the order, click again on the column header.","Change the row order in the Validation window","ChangetheroworderintheValidationwindow.htm");
Page[143]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The validation service prevents the runtime object from being created from the business object if the business object is invalid. Component warnings and errors are displayed in the Validation window.","The Validation window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view.","To change the column order in the Validation window","In the Validation window, drag and drop the required column header to the required column using your mouse.","The column order will be changed.","Change the column order in the Validation window","ChangethecolumnorderintheValidationwindow.htm");
Page[144]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The validation service prevents the runtime object from being created from the business object if the business object is invalid. Component warnings and errors are displayed in the Validation window.","The Validation window can be customized; the user can change the row order, change the column order and remove or add columns from view.","To remove or add columns in the Validation window","In the Validation window, click on the @ button. The Change Visible Columns dialog will be initiated.","In the Change Visible Columns dialog, tick the appropriate boxes to remove or add columns from view. Only the columns ticked will display in the Validation window.","Click on the OK button.","The columns ticked will display in the Validation window.","Remove or add columns in the Validation window","RemoveoraddcolumnsintheValidationwindow.htm");
Page[145]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The validation service prevents the runtime object from being created from the business object if the business object is invalid. Component warnings and errors are displayed in the Validation window.","Validation can be done in many ways;","From the Main menu ","From the Main tool bar","In the Explorer window","When the Validation task is running the progress can be viewed.","To view a running validation task","Whilst the validation service is running the progress can be viewed in the progress bar located at the bottom of the Validation window.","To view the validation tasks as they run, click on the progress bar to expand the list of running tasks. ","Another validation progress bar will be initiated.  The name of each item being validated will be shown as the validation against it runs;","The validation process will continue to run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","View a running validation task","Viewarunningvalidationtask.htm");
Page[146]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The validation service prevents the runtime object from being created from the business object if the business object is invalid. Component warnings and errors are displayed in the Validation window.","Validation can be done in many ways;","From the Main menu ","From the Main tool bar","In the Explorer window","When the Validation task is running the progress can be cancelled.","To cancel a running validation task","Whilst the validation service is running the progress can be viewed in the progress bar located at the bottom of the Validation window.","To cancel the validation task, click on the @ icon to the right of the progress bar.","The Cancel Running Task dialog will be initiated. Click on the Yes button to cancel the validation progress.","The Validation window will remain empty. ","Cancel a running validation task","Cancelarunningvalidationtask.htm");
Page[147]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The user may validate a Solution from the Explorer window.","To validate a Solution","In the Explorer window, select the Solution that you wish to validate.","Right click and select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validate a Solution","ValidateaSolution_1.htm");
Page[148]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","The user may validate a Folder from the Explorer window.","To validate a Folder ","In the Explorer window, select the Folder that you wish to validate.","Right click and select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validate a Folder","ValidateaFolder_1.htm");
Page[149]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","Validating a component automatically validates any referenced or embedded components.","The user may validate a Component from the Main Menu or the Main tool bar. On doing this, any changes made to the component in an open editor that have not yet been saved will be taken into account during validation. ","To validate a component from the Main Menu","You must have the component you wish to validate open in the Main editor and in focus.","From the Main menu bar, click on File.","From the drop-down list select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","To validate a component from the Main tool bar","You must have the component you wish to validate open in the Main editor and in focus.","From the Main tool bar, click on @ icon.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","The user may validate a component in the Explorer window. On doing this, any changes made to the component in an open editor will not be taken into account and the validation will be performed on the user/shared area component. ","To validate a component from the Explorer window","In the Explorer window, select the Component that you wish to validate.","Right click and select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validate a Component","ValidateaComponent_1.htm");
Page[150]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","Validation can be done in many ways;","From the Main menu ","From the Main tool bar","In the Explorer window","The user may validate a Component from the Main menu.","To validate from the Main menu","You must have the component you wish to validate open in the Main editor and in focus.","From the Main menu bar, click on File.","From the drop-down list select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validation from the Main menu","ValidationfromtheMainmenu.htm");
Page[151]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","Validation can be done in many ways;","From the Main menu ","From the Main tool bar","In the Explorer window","The user may validate a Component from the Main tool bar.","To validate from the Main tool bar","You must have the component you wish to validate open in the Main editor and in focus.","From the Main tool bar, click on @ icon.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window. If errors in the open editor are found, the area column of the validation window will show an active editor icon to indicate that it is not the saved version of a component that is being validated.","Validation from the Main tool bar","ValidationfromtheMaintoolbar.htm");
Page[152]=new Array("Validation is a service that carries out a check on the validity of a Solution, a Folder or a Component and its contents.","Validation can be done in many ways;","From the Main menu ","From the Main tool bar","In the Explorer window","The user may validate a Solution, a Folder or a Component from the Explorer window.","To validate from the Explorer window","In the Explorer window, select the Solution, Folder or Component that you wish to validate.","Right click and select Validate.","The validation process will run and the results will be displayed in the Validation window.","Validation from the Explorer window","ValidationfromtheExplorerwindow.htm");
Page[153]=new Array("The Search Results window when activated, displays in the Output area of the user interface. The window displays the returned results from an Advanced Search.","Advance Search can be initiated from the Main menu bar and has a basic and an advanced option. ","The Advanced Search function (basic and advanced) allows the user to search components details for the following;","Words, Phrases, Dates, Users, Component types and Component states.","The Advanced Search function (basic and advanced) enables the user to search for components in solutions only. ","Search Results overview","SearchResultsoverview.htm");
Page[154]=new Array("The Advanced Search function allows the user to search components details for the following: Words, Phrases, Dates, Users, Component types and Component states.","Advanced Search can be initiated from the Main menu bar and has a basic and an advanced option.","The Advanced Search function (basic and advanced) enables the user to search for components in solutions only.","Any returned search results from an Advanced Search (basic or advanced) will be returned and displayed in the Search window located in the Output area of the user interface.","The user can perform some actions by right clicking on a component row in the window. The actions available depend upon the component type. Available actions are the same as the actions available in the Explorer window; please see the Explorer window help page for further information. Double clicking on a component in the Component column will open the component in the Main editor.","The user can customise this window:","A  user can change the column order by clicking on a column header and dragging into the preferred place. ","@ Filter: Use this button to display or remove the Filter bar at the bottom of the window. The user can use the filter field to filter for specific words.","@ Change visible columns: Use this button to choose which column to view. The user can remove or add columns from view using the Change Visible Columns button.This is only visible in the window when the Filter field is visible. This is also available on right click in the column header.","The following columns are available:","Component: This column displays the Component name.  ","@ Area state: This column displays the domain that the component sits in.  @ indicates that the component sits in a user domain.  @ indicates that the component sits in a shared domain.","Author: This column displays the author/creator of the component.","@ Broken state: This column displays the broken state of a component. @ indicates that there are no publishing rules defined between the component and a dependant component. If the field is empty, the component is not broken.","@ Component state: This column displays the component state.  @ indicates a new component.  @ indicates a modified component. If the field is empty, the component is unmodified.  ","@ Conflict state: This column displays the conflict state of the component. @ indicates that there is a conflict. If the field is empty, there is no conflict.    ","Creation date: This column displays the date the Component was created. ","@ Favourite state: This column displays any components that the user has marked as a favourite.","@ Lock state: This column displays the Lock/Unlock status of the component. @  indicates that the component is locked. If the field is empty, the component is not locked. ","Locked by: This column displays the user name of the user currently locking the component.","Name: This column displays the Name that has been given to the component.","Path: This column allows the user to display the full path of a component.","@ Revision shared area: This column displays the version number of the component on the shared domain.","@ Revision user area: This column displays the version number of the component on the user domain.","Type: This column displays the Component Type (Decision Process Flow, Call Interface Manager, etc.)","Update Author: This column displays the author responsible for the latest update of the component.","Update date: This column displays the last date that the component was updated.","Search Results window","SearchResultswindow.htm");
Page[155]=new Array("By default, the Palette area is displayed down the right hand side of the User Interface.","The Palette area houses the following windows:","The Palette window.","The Resources window.","The Properties window.","By default on opening the software the Palette area is empty.","The Palette window will be displayed when there is a palette of system resources available for the component being edited or when initiated from the Main menu bar. ","The Resources window will be displayed when there is a resources window available for the component being edited or when initiated from the Main menu bar. Only resources created by the user will be available in the Resources window. ","The Properties window will be displayed when properties for the item selected are available. The Properties window can be initiated from the Main menu bar.","Palette area","Palettearea.htm");
Page[156]=new Array("The Palette contains a list of system resources that are available for use in the active editor. The user can drag and drop resources from the Palette window into a component being edited in the Main editor. The content of the Palette is directly related to the type of editor open in the Main editor, the capability of the user's particular software, together with the access rights of the user. ","By default, on opening the software the Palette window is housed in the Palette area. The Palette area is displayed down the right hand side of the interface.","If the editor does not require the user to use any resources, or an editor is not open in the Main editor, the Palette area will empty.","Palette overview","Paletteoverview.htm");
Page[157]=new Array("The Palette window contains a list of system resources that are available for use in the active editor. The user can drag and drop resources from the Palette window into the component being edited in the Main editor. The content of the Palette is directly related to the type of editor open in the Main editor, the capability of the user's particular software, together with the access rights of the user.","By default, on opening the software the Palette window is housed in the Palette area. The Palette area is displayed down the right hand side of the interface.","If the Palette window has been closed, it can be reopened again at any time. Please see the Initiate the Palette window help page for more information on this.","There are some options available on right clicking on a component in the Palette:","Refresh Palette - This refreshes the Palette.","Hide Item Names - Hides the component names, leaving the icons displayed. The option to Show item names will be given on right click.","Show Big Icons -  Enlarges the Icons. The option to Show Small Icons will be given on right click.","Reset Palette - Contracts the expanded view. The Confirm Palette Reset dialog will display. Click on the OK button to confirm reset.","Palette Manager - Allows customisation of the Palette content. The Palette Manager dialog will display. Once customisation is complete click on the Close button to confirm changes.","Palette window","Palettewindow.htm");
Page[158]=new Array("The Palette contains a list of system resources that are available for use in the active editor. ","By default, on opening the software the Palette window is housed in the Palette area. The Palette area is displayed down the right hand side of the interface.","If the Palette window has been closed, it can be reopened again at any time.","To initiate the Palette window","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select Palette.","The Palette window is displayed.","Initiate the Palette window","InitiatethePalettewindow.htm");
Page[159]=new Array("The Resources window contains a list of resources that are available for use in the active editor; components that are relevant, components that are visible from the folder of the component being edited or components in another folder that are published to it. Please see the Publishing overview for more information. ","The user can drag and drop resources from the Resources window into the component being edited in the Main editor. The content of the Resources window is directly related to the type of editor open in the Main editor along with the access rights of the user.","Components in italics are located in a different folder to the component being edited and are available for use because they have been published to this location.","By default, on opening the software the Resources window is housed in the Palette area. The Palette area is displayed down the right hand side of the interface.","If the editor does not require the user to use any resources, or an editor is not open, the Resources window will be empty.","Resources overview","Resourcesoverview.htm");
Page[160]=new Array("The Resources window contains a list of resources that are available for use in the active editor; components that are relevant, components that are visible from the folder of the component being edited or components in another folder that are published to it. Please see the Publishing overview for more information. ","The user can drag and drop resources from the Resources window into the component being edited in the Main editor. The content of the Resources window is directly related to the type of editor open in the Main editor along with the access rights of the user. ","Components in italics are located in a different folder to the component being edited and are available for use because they have been published to this location.","By default, on opening the software the Resources window is housed in the Palette area. The Palette area is displayed down the right hand side of the interface.","If the Resources window has been closed, it can be reopened again at any time. Please see the Initiate the Resources window help page for more information on this.","Resources window","Resourceswindow.htm");
Page[161]=new Array("By default, on opening the software the Resources window is housed in the Palette area. The Palette area is displayed down the right hand side of the interface.","If the Resources window has been closed, it can be reopened again at any time.","To initiate the Resources window","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select Resources window.","The Resources window is displayed.","Initiate the Resources window","InitiatetheResourceswindow.htm");
Page[162]=new Array("Properties are the characteristics of a Repository, Domain, Solution, Folder, Component or Decision Process Flow node.","The detailed properties of any selected Repository, Domain, Solution, Folder, Component or Decision Process Flow node can be displayed in the Properties window. The properties displayed will depend upon the item selected.","Properties can include any of the following:","URI","Framework ID","Creation date","GUID","Revision shared domain","Update date","UUID","Revision user domain","Systems","Name","Lock state","Component state","Type","Locked by","Conflict state","Domains","Author","Obsolete state","Domain ID","Update Author","Node Reference Type","Repository ID","Root folder ID","Reference Artifact","By default, on opening the software the Properties window is not displayed. Once initiated it is housed in the Palette area. Please see the initiate the Properties window help page for more information on this. ","Properties overview","Propertiesoverview.htm");
Page[163]=new Array("The detailed properties of any selected Repository, Domain, Solution, Folder, Component or Decision Process Flow Node can be displayed in the Properties window. The properties displayed will depend upon the item selected. ","By default, on opening the software the Properties window is not displayed. Once initiated it is housed in the Palette area. Please see the initiate the Properties window help page for more information on this.","If the Properties window has been closed, it can be reopened again at any time. Please see the Initiate the Properties window help page for more information on this.","Clicking on the @ icon next to a property will display the property value in a Properties dialog. Once viewed, click on the Close button to close the dialog.","There are some options available on right-clicking inside the Properties window:","Sort by category -  Sorts rows in alphabetical order of the properties column.","Sort by name - Sorts rows in alphabetical order of the values column.","Show Description Area - Populates the bottom area of the Properties window. The user can select a row and the value is displayed in the bottom area of the Properties window.  Appropriate Help pages can be activated by clicking on the @ Icon.","Properties window","Propertieswindow.htm");
Page[164]=new Array("The detailed properties of any selected Repository, Domain, Solution, Folder, Component or Decision Process Flow node can be displayed in the Properties window.","By default, on opening the software the Properties window is not displayed. Once Initiated it is housed in the Palette area.  ","If the Properties window has been closed, it can be reopened again at any time.","To initiate the Properties window","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select Properties.","The Properties window is displayed. You will now be able to select display the properties for any Repository, Domain, Folder, Component or Decision Process Flow node.","Initiate the Properties window","InitiatethePropertieswindow.htm");
Page[165]=new Array("The detailed properties of any selected Repository, Domain, Solution, Folder, Component or Decision Process Flow Node can be displayed in the Properties window. The properties displayed will depend upon the item selected. ","The user can view the properties.","To display properties","In the Main system view, initiate the Properties window.","To view the properties for a repository, click on the required repository in the Explorer window. The Properties window will be populated with the property detail for the repository.","To view the properties for a domain, click on the required domain in the Explorer window. The Properties window will be populated with the property detail for the domain.","To view the properties for a solution, click on the required solution in the Explorer window. The Properties window will be populated with the property detail for the solution.","To view the properties for a folder, click on the required folder in the Explorer window. The Properties window will be populated with the property detail for the folder.","To view the properties for a component, click on the required component in the Explorer window. The Properties window will be populated with the property detail for the component.","To view the properties for a decision process flow node, click on the required node in the Decision Process Flow editor. The Properties window will be populated with the property detail for the node.","Display Properties","DisplayProperties.htm");
Page[166]=new Array("By default on opening the software,  the User Interface is displayed in a predefined position.","The User Interface consists of six areas. ","The Main menu bar area within the User Interface is fixed and can not be customized or moved.","The Main tool bar area is fixed within the User Interface; the elements of the tool bar can be customized.","Four of the areas have independent windows that can be resized, maximized, minimized, undocked, docked, closed, opened and relocated to different positions within the User Interface. This enables the user to customize the view of the system:","The Main editor area - This area houses the Main editor by default. The Main editor can be resized, maximized, minimized, undocked, docked, closed, opened and relocated to different positions within the User Interface.","The Explorer area - This area houses the Explorer window, the Server Connections window, the Navigator window, the Satellite View window, the Where Used window and the Strategy Viewer window by default. All of these windows can be resized, maximized, minimized, undocked, docked, closed, opened and relocated to different positions within the User Interface.","The Output area - This area houses the History window, the Inventory window, the Validation window, Search Results window and the Output window by default. All of these windows can be resized, maximized, minimized, undocked, docked, closed, opened and relocated to different positions within the User Interface.","The Palette area - This area houses the Palette window, the Resources window and the Properties window by default. These windows can be resized, maximized, minimized, undocked, docked, closed, opened and relocated to different positions within the User Interface.","The user also has the ability to reset the User Interface to its original view.","If a window is not visible in the User Interface, the user can initiate a window from the Main menu bar. Please see the Initiate a window from the Main menu bar help page for more information on this.","View Options overview","ViewOptionsoverview.htm");
Page[167]=new Array("By default on opening the software,  the user interface is displayed in a predefined position.","Four of the areas have independent windows that can be resized, maximized, minimized, undocked, docked, closed, opened and relocated to different positions within the user interface. This enables the user to customize the view of the system:","The Main editor area - This area houses the Main editor by default.","The Explorer area - This area houses the Explorer window, the Server Connections Manager window, the Navigator window, the Satellite View window, the Where Used window and the Strategy Viewer window by default.","The Output area - This area houses the History window, the Inventory window, the Validation window, the Search Results window and the Output window by default.","The Palette area - This area houses the Palette window, the Resources window and the Properties window by default.","To customize the User Interface view","In the window you wish to close, maximize, minimize, undock, or dock, right click on the window tab located at the top of the window.","A drop-down list will be activated.","To close a window, select Close Window. The window will disappear from view. The window can be initiated from the Main menu bar at any time.","To maximize a window, select Maximize Window. The window will fill the screen. The window can be maximized at any time.","To minimize a window, select Minimize Window. The window will revert to its previous size and in its previous location.","To undock a window, select Undock Window. The window is now a floating window and you can now drag the window to a desired location in the User Interface or anywhere on your screen. ","To dock an undocked window, select Dock Window. The window will dock to its original location.","To resize a window, move the cursor along the edge of a window until the @ icon is displayed and drag the arrow in the required direction until the window is the required size.","To change the user interface to display the Main editor and the Palette and Resources windows only, double click on the Main editor tab. To return back to original display, double click on the Main editor tab.","The User Interface view can be reset at any time. Please see the reset the User Interface view help pages for more information on this.","A user can also click on the Minimize Window @ icon in the window tab to minimize the window. The name of the window will be displayed in a vertical bar to the left or the right of the user interface. To maximize the window, click on the appropriate tab in the vertical bar. The window will return to its location, click on the pin @ icon in the corner of the window to keep it in place.","Individual windows may also be dragged and dropped to any other location in the user interface. Simply click in the window tab and drag to the required location and drop.","Any of the windows can be closed by clicking on the @ in the window tab.","Customize the User Interface view","CustomizetheUserInterfaceview.htm");
Page[168]=new Array("By default on opening the software,  the user interface is displayed in a predefined position.","Four of the areas have independent windows that can be resized, maximized, minimized, undocked, docked, closed, opened and relocated to different positions within the user interface. This enables the user to customize the view of the system.","The User Interface view can be reset at any time.","To reset the User Interface view","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select Reset Windows.","The User Interface will reopen and windows can be reopened as appropriate. Once reopened they will be displayed in their default positions. Please see the Initiate a window from the Main menu bar help topic for more information on this.","Reset the User Interface view","ResettheUserInterfaceview.htm");
Page[169]=new Array("If a window is not visible in the User Interface, the user can initiate it from the Main menu bar.","You will be unable to initiate the Satellite View window from the Main menu. The Satellite View window is only initiated when the Decision Process Flow or Decision Setter components are open in the Main editor. It is also initiated when the user is publishing. ","To initiate a window from the Main menu bar","In the main system view, click on Window in the Main menu bar and select the name of the window you wish to initiate.","The window will display in the default predefined position in the User Interface.","Initiate a window from the Main menu bar","InitiateawindowfromtheMainmenubar.htm");
Page[170]=new Array("The user can undo modifications made in the editor by clicking on the @ icon in the Main tool bar.","Undo is only available for some specific actions:","Actions that change the state of a component","Navigating within the tabs of the main editor ","Navigating between views of embedded components","Undo is not available for actions that change how a component is displayed, for example:","Zoom in the matrix","Changing how the information in the cells are displayed in the matrix","<br>The user can undo up to the last 100 actions per component in a current session. Actions performed on embedded components count against this limit: ","Open Scorecard A that contains an embedded class set.","Opening the class set will count as one change. ","Adding a row to the class set will count as a second change.","Closing the class set will count as a third change to Scorecard A.","Opening a component referenced in Scorecard A, through the scorecard editor, and making changes will not count against the limit for Scorecard A","Opening Scorecard B and making changes will not count against the limit of 100 changes for Scorecard A.","The undo option may be cleared if a referenced component is changed (i.e. by reference class set has been changed or made in a matrix editor) because the stored changes may invalidate the state of the undo actions. The Undo icon will be inactive if the undo history is empty.","If the undo action is not available in an editor the icon will be inactive.","Undo","Undo.htm");
Page[171]=new Array("The redo option is activated after the first undo action is performed.","The user can redo undone modifications in the editor by clicking on the @ icon in the Main tool bar.","Redo is only available for actions that have been undone. The user can redo the last 100 undo actions per component, including actions performed on its embedded components: ","Open a component and make change A and then change B, then undo change B.","Both the undo and the redo buttons are activated.","You can choose to redo change B that you have just undone, or to undo change A.","If you make another change to the component or save it, the redo button is disabled and all changes that have been undone are removed.","The redo option may be cleared if a referenced component is changed (i.e. by reference class set has been changed or made in a matrix editor) ; the stored changes may invalidate the state of the redo actions. Once the component is saved, or another change is made, the redo history is cleared. The Redo icon will be inactive if the redo history is empty.","If the redo action is not available in an editor the icon will be inactive.","Redo","Redo.htm");
Page[172]=new Array("Content Management enables the user to create templates that can be distributed to other users. ","Templates are a snapshot of a part of the repository. They can be a single component, multiple components, or even folder structures with all the associated publishing rules and allowed types.","Once templates have been created, they can be copied, renamed, marked as &quot;favourite&quot;, deleted or exported, but they can not be edited.","Templates are stored in a Content repository and have a small icon to identify them as templates; so, for example, the decision process flow icon is  @  while the template icon is  @. ","There are two basic types of templates:","Folder/solution templates - contain all the information needed to recreate the folder structure, complete with allowed types and publishing rules. They do not have to contain components.","Component templates - created from a single component. However, the template contains all the components referenced by or embedded within the main component. When the template is applied, all the referenced and embedded components are created as well.","See Create a template from a folder or solution and Create a template from a component for details on these types of templates.","Special access permissions are required to create and apply templates. See Access permissions for more information.","It is important to remember that, to create and apply templates, the Content repository must be properly set up and loaded. See Create and load a content solution for details on how to do this.","Content Management overview","ContentManagementoverview.htm");
Page[173]=new Array("To create and apply templates, the user must have a Security Profile that includes a Functional Role of the Repository Type &quot;Content&quot; (as opposed to the &quot;Solution&quot; role); furthermore, the ability to create templates requires a &quot;Create&quot; permission within the role, while the ability to apply templates requires a &quot;Read&quot; permission. ","To apply folder and solution templates the user is also required to have Architect permissions, as they will be creating folders when applying templates. ","Creating and applying templates is similar to the export/import functionality; however, import/export is more restrictive as the user cannot redirect folders during import, and only users with Solution Administrator permission can import.","Access permissions","Accesspermissions.htm");
Page[174]=new Array("License credentials are included as part of the template when folder/solution templates and component templates are created. ","License credentials are set up for a folder the first time it is created by a template. Applying templates subsequently will not change existing credentials in a folder. So once a folder has been created, applying any number of other templates will not change the existing license credentials.","However, if templates containing components of a new type are applied to an existing folder (either by applying a folder/solution template or a component template), then the license credentials for the new component type will be set up for the folder.","License credentials","Licensecredentials.htm");
Page[175]=new Array("When creating a template from a component, such as a scorecard, that is linked to a particular data model, that data model will be treated as a dependency of the scorecard. When the scorecard template is applied, the data model will be applied as well. The user must link to that exact data model, or the scorecard will not work; it is not simply the structure and attributes of the data model that are important, but the underlying identifications of the characteristics themselves. ","If the exact data set already exists in the solution into which the template is being applied, the user can link to it. ","Note that all dependent logical data sources are stored in a template, not just the characteristics used by the components.","Templates and data models","Templatesanddatamodels.htm");
Page[176]=new Array("The user must create content folders for the various types of templates that will be created. It may be helpful, for example, to store scorecards and class sets in separate folders. Creating a new content folder is like creating a new solution folder, except that the allowed types are all templates rather than components.","If the user wants to have the ability to create or apply solution templates they will need to have &quot;Solution&quot; configured as one of the Component types in their Content repository. It is the only component type listed under the Solutions category in the Functional Roles editor.","To create a content folder","From the content repository, right click on a content solution and select Add folder. The Add folder dialog is displayed.","Click the @ button to add component template types from the left pane to the list of Allowed component types in the right pane:","Click on the OK button to create the folder.","Now, when you create templates, only templates of the allowed type can be added to this folder. Furthermore, when you create a template of a different type, this folder will not even appear in the Save &lt;component&gt; As Template dialog.","Create content folders","Createcontentfolders.htm");
Page[177]=new Array("Component templates are created from a single component. However, the template contains all the components referenced by or embedded within the main component. When the template is applied, all the referenced and embedded components are created as well.","Component templates","Componenttemplates.htm");
Page[178]=new Array("The user can create templates from individual components.","To create templates, the user must have a Security Profile that includes a Functional Role assigned the Repository Type &quot;Content&quot; in addition to a Functional Role assigned the Repository Type &quot;Solution&quot;. The user must also have Read access to the component.","To create a template from a component","In the Explorer window, load a Content Solution within the Content Repository.","In the Solution Repository, navigate to and right click on the component from which to create the template and select Save As Template. The Save &lt;component&gt; As Template dialog is displayed. ","Only those content folders that allow the type of component from which you are creating a template are displayed.","In the following example, we are creating a scorecard template:","Select the content folder in which to store the template.","Type a name for the template in the Name field.","A red cross may still be displayed.","Hover next to the red validation cross. A tooltip will be displayed that informs you of any problems that may still be occurring.","Once any issues have been resolved, add a description; this description is displayed when the template is consumed. ","Click on the OK button to send the template job to the Job Submission Console for execution.","The Remote Job Notification dialog will be initiated.","Click on the OK button to launch the Job Submission Console.","The Job Submission Console will be initiated in the Main editor area of the user interface.","Once the job has run to completion, the template is displayed in the Explorer window, under the content solution, in the selected folder:","The template cannot be edited; it can only be copied, renamed, marked as favourite, deleted or exported.","Create a template from a component","Createatemplatefromacomponent.htm");
Page[179]=new Array("The Save ... As Template dialog enables the user to create templates from individual components, or from a folder or solution. ","The dialog consists of:","Name - the name of the template to be created.","Content Gallery - displays content folders where the template may be stored. Only those content folders that allow the type(s) of component(s) from which the user is creating a template are displayed.","Document Link - a user-entered external link to a web page so the user can subsequently view extra information from the digital library.","Description - a user-entered description of the template; this description is displayed when the template is applied.","When the user clicks on the OK button, the template job is sent to the Job Submission Console for execution.","Save Component As Template dialog","SaveComponentAsTemplatedialog.htm");
Page[180]=new Array("A component template may consist of a single component, or it may include any number of dependencies. The contents of applied templates are linked to the existing solution dynamically; if the appropriate structure is already in place, the Consume Template Job identifies where each component should logically reside. The user is given the option of overriding this assumption.","A component template includes all its required components but does not preserve any folder structure. All the required components are created in the target folder (except as noted below).","If a component template is applied into a solution that contains some or many of the same components, the system will link dynamically to the existing components.","Only templates for existing allowed types can be added to a folder. The user will be prompted to map components of other types to a different folder. This does not create publishing rules and the components will be created &#8220;broken&#8221;.","When adding from a template, the main component can not be created with the same name as an existing component. Any existing components with the same name and type will not be overwritten and the references will be updated (this may cause some of the new components to be created &#8220;broken&#8221;).","If there are any existing dependent components with the same name but a different type, the user will be prompted to map them to a different folder.  This does not create publishing rules and the components may be created &#8220;broken&#8221; if appropriate publishing rules are not in place.","Applied templates create new components entirely within the user domain, where they can be manipulated and modified without affecting the shared repository.","No validation of the publishing rules for folders is performed during this process; however, there is validation against allowed types and the Create permissions.","To apply a component template","Start by having a content solution loaded.","Right click on the folder in the Solution Repository where you want to create the component, and select Add from template. The Add From Template dialog is displayed.","Select the template from which to create the component.","Add a name for the new component, and select a template from the Content Gallery.","If the component has dependencies, the Configure button is enabled. ","To review or reconfigure the component paths, click on the Configure button to display the Configure Targets for &lt;component&gt; dialog.","To reconfigure the target location for any folder or component, click on the Helper icon @ to display the Map &lt;component&gt; to Existing Folder dialog.","If the user remaps components, they must ensure that they are remapping to folders they have permissions for, and that will accept that type of component. If the user is remapping a folder that contains many subfolders, for example, the user can check the &quot;Update target folder and sub-folders&quot; tickbox to update all subfolders and components within those subfolders from the selected folder down.","Select the folder to map the component or folder to, and click on the OK button. ","Continue to map components and folders, then click on the OK button to exit the Configure Targets dialog and return to the Add From Template dialog.","Click on the OK button to send the Consume Template Job to the Job Submission Console.","Once the job has run to completion, the new component or components are displayed in the Explorer window, under the solution:","The components are created in the user domain, and thus appear in green by default. Any folders created by the Consume Template Job are created in the shared domain.","Apply a component template","Applyacomponenttemplate.htm");
Page[181]=new Array("The Add From Template dialog is initiated during the &quot;Apply a component template&quot; process and enables the user to select a template to apply from the Content Gallery.","The dialog consists of:","Name - if a component template, provide the name of the new component. If a folder or solution template, the name field is greyed out since the contents of the template are to be applied without modification.","Content Gallery - displays templates that can be applied; templates displayed are compatible with the allowed types for the folder into which the template will be applied.","Document Link - displays an external link to a web page so the user can view extra information from the digital library.","Description - displays a description of the selected template.","Configure - if a component template the button is enabled if the selected component has dependencies. Click to display the Configure Targets for &lt;component&gt; dialog. If a folder or solution template, button is disabled since the folder structure is created as determined by the original folder or solution.","Please see the Apply a component template help topic for more information on this.","Add From Template dialog","AddFromTemplatedialog.htm");
Page[182]=new Array("The Configure Targets for &lt;component&gt; dialog is initiated during the &quot;Apply a component template&quot; process and enables the user to review or reconfigure the paths of any folders or components that are created when a component template is applied.  ","The destination path names are displayed for each folder and component that will be created. Full path information is displayed as a tool tip, by hovering the cursor over the target path name.","If the user remaps components, they must ensure that they are remapping to folders they have permissions for, and that will accept that type of component.","Note in the example above that two of the mappings have created errors, as marked by the @ icon. Hovering the cursor over the icon will display the relevant error message: ","Please see the Apply a component template help topic for more information on this.","Configure Targets for &lt;component&gt; dialog","ConfigureTargetsfor_component_dialog.htm");
Page[183]=new Array("The Map &lt;component&gt; to Existing Folder dialog is initiated during the &quot;Apply a component template&quot; process and enables the user to reconfigure the target location for any folder or component.","For each folder or component listed in the Configure Targets for &lt;component&gt; dialog, the system will try to identify where each component should logically reside. The user is given the option of overriding this assumption.","Please see the Apply a component template help topic for more information on this.","Map &lt;component&gt; to Existing Folder dialog","Map_component_toExistingFolderdialog.htm");
Page[184]=new Array("Folder and solution templates contain all the information needed to recreate the folder structure, complete with allowed types and publishing rules. They do not have to contain components.","Folder/solution templates","solutiontemplates.htm");
Page[185]=new Array("The user can create templates from folders or solutions. Folder and solution level templates recreate the folder structure, include all allowed types for each folder and all publishing rules, and bring all components into the structure. Internal relationships between components are maintained by pathnames and unique component identifiers.","Templates created from folders and solutions are the same thing, have the same icon @ and can be used to create new folder substructures or whole solutions.","Empty folder and solution level templates can also be created; these are useful when creating a folder structure within a solution that can then be used when applying component templates or other folder templates. Empty folder and solution level templates retain the publishing rules and allowed types. ","To create templates, the user must have a Security Profile that includes a Functional Role assigned the Repository Type &quot;Content&quot; in addition to a Functional Role assigned the Repository Type &quot;Solution&quot;.","To create a template from a folder or solution","Start by having a content solution loaded.","Right click on the folder or solution from which to create the template, and select Save as template. The Save &lt;folder or solution&gt; As Template dialog is displayed.","If you want the ability to create solution templates you will need to have &quot;Solution&quot; configured as one of the Component types in your Content repository. It is the only component type listed under the Solutions category in the Functional Roles editor.","At this time, creation of folder templates is restricted to folders that contain all dependent components within the one folder; if any components in a folder have dependent components in other folders, you cannot create a folder template from that folder.","Type a name in the Name field.","From the Content Gallery select the content folder in which to store it.","Type in an external link to a web page so the user can subsequently view extra information from the digital library.","Type a description in the Description field; this description is displayed when the template is applied.","Click on the OK button to send the template job to the Job Submission Console for execution.","Click on the OK button to launch the Job Submission Console.","Once the job has run to completion, the template is displayed in the Explorer window, under the content solution:","The template cannot be edited; it can only be copied, renamed, marked as favourite, deleted or exported.","Create a template from a folder or solution","Createatemplatefromafolderorsolution.htm");
Page[186]=new Array("Applying folder and solution level templates recreates the folder structure, including all allowed types for each folder and all publishing rules and brings all the components into the structure. Internal relationships between components are maintained by pathnames and unique component identifiers.","Folder publishing rules will be merged with existing publishing rules; i.e., any rules present in the template that are not present in the existing folder structure will be added to the folder structure.","The apply process will add any required allowed types to existing folders; any new folders will be created with all the allowed types specified in the template.","If a template contains any empty folders and solutions they will also be created; they are useful when creating a folder structure within a solution that can then be used when applying component templates or other folder templates. Empty folders and solutions retain the publishing rules and allowed types.","Applied templates create new components entirely within the user domain, where they can be manipulated and modified without affecting the shared repository.","To apply templates, the user will need to have Architect permissions if folders must be created when the template is applied. The alternative is to have the necessary folder structure in place before applying the template.","To apply a folder or solution template","Start by having a content solution loaded.","Right click on the folder in the Solution Repository where you want the folder or solution structure to be created, and select Add from template. The Add From Template dialog is displayed.","Select a template from the Content Gallery:","The Name field is greyed out after the user selects a template from the Content Gallery, since the contents of the template are to be applied without modification. ","The Configure button is disabled, since the folder structure is created as determined by the original folder or solution. Note that the full original folder structure does not have to exist prior to applying a template (as it does when importing an export file); the applied folder structure will be created entirely, rooted in the folder you initially selected in step 2.","Click on the OK button to send the Consume Template Job to the Job Submission Console.","Once the job has run to completion, the contents of the folder are displayed in the Explorer window in the folder or solution into which they were applied:","The components are created in the user domain, and thus appear in green by default. Any folders created by the Consume Template Job are created in the shared domain.","Apply a folder or solution template","Applyafolderorsolutiontemplate.htm");
Page[187]=new Array("A user with Architect permission can create and load an empty content solution within which to create templates. To do so, the user might need to first create a domain within a repository. A solution can then be added.","Create and load an empty content solution","In the Explorer window, right click on the appropriate repository. ","Select Connect.","You can also double click on the Repository to connect.","The Repository name turns blue to show that you are connected to it.","Right click on the required content repository.","Select New.","In the New dialog, select Empty domain and click on the OK button.","The new domain will be listed within the selected repository.","Right click on the domain.","Select New.","In the New dialog, select Empty solution and click on the OK button.","Select Add solution.","In the Add solution dialog, type the name of the new solution.","Click on the OK button.","The solution will be added to the domain.","Right click on the solution and select Load solution.","You can also double click on the solution to connect.","You can now click on  the @ icon to open the Solution.","You are now ready to use the content solution to create solution and folder templates. See Create content folders for more information on how to further configure the repository.","Create and load an empty content solution","Createandloadanemptycontentsolution.htm");
Page[188]=new Array("The Export/Import functionality enables any user with read permission to export components, folders or entire solutions along with their dependencies. Users with the Solution Administrator or Architect functional role as part of their security profile will be able to import the exported components or folders into a new or existing solution. The import functionality is also used to add pre-configured domains and solutions to a repository, as described in the Explorer overview.","Import and export are available for all three repository types: Content, Reporting and Solution. The solution signature is included in the import and export. ","The Export job will include all required folder structures from the domain level down to the folder or component to be exported. So, for example; if the user is exporting a single component (such as a scorecard, as in the example below), the export job will include the selected component along with its referenced components, as well as the folders that contain the selected component and the referenced components, all the way up to the solution level (the domain level is not shown in the export view).","In this example, the Post-Bureau Risk Scorecard was selected for export:","The Export job finds and includes all components referenced by the selected scorecard. The same is true when exporting a folder; the Export job will include the selected folder and the folders that contain any referenced components. ","The Import job will import the identical structure into the new or existing solution. The only difference is that the solution name will be the name of the solution into which the folders and components are being imported. The Import job resolves all references automatically. Imported components are checked in to the repository as part of the import process.","If an import contains any components which already exist is the solution, the user has the option to overwrite those components with the component data contained in the import file. If the user chooses to overwrite, the import job will check out the pre-existing components to the user's user domain and overwrite the user domain versions of the pre-existing components. If the user chooses not to overwrite, those components will not be imported and any references to those components will be resolved to the pre-existing shared domain components.","Allowed types","The exported document stores lists of allowed types for each folder that is exported (even if no components of that type are exported). When importing, any missing folders are automatically created with the appropriate full list of allowed types.","If a folder already exists, only the required allowed type will be added if missing and required for the purpose of the import. ","License Credentials","License credentials are exported with the components, folders and solutions in the export file. ","Whenever a new folder is created on import, as when the original export was created at the solution or folder level, the license credentials for that folder are read in from the export file. ","Importing an XML file which was created from a solution or folder level export will override credentials within an existing folder; however, importing a component level export will not override credentials for components of that type in an existing folder. If a component of a new type is imported into an existing folder (ie, a component for which credentials have not been declared), the license credentials for the new component type will be read into the folder. ","For legacy export files (those without preset license credentials), the default license credentials on import are the same as for any newly created folder.","The user will have the option of updating the license credentials for existing allowed types.","Publishing rules","The exported document stores all publishing rules for each folder that is exported (even if a folder referenced by a publishing relationship is not itself exported). When importing the solution, any folders which are automatically created have all the associated publishing rules configured for that folder (in all directions). ","Publishing rules are also included for any dependent component folders. ","When importing, publishing rules are also created linking any pre-existing folders to the new ones where appropriate. So, if a publishing rule is imported with a folder, it can create a publishing relationship with an existing folder where that publishing relationship did not previously exist.","Export/Import has functionality in common with the creation and consumption of templates. The main difference is that only users with the Solution Administrator or Architect functional role as part of their security profile will be able to create an Import job, and Import can only be performed at the solution level.","Export/Import overview","Importoverview.htm");
Page[189]=new Array("The user can export a component, folder or solution along with any dependant components and folder structures, from within the Explorer window. The export process creates an Export job in the Job Submission Console.","To export a component, folder or solution","In the Explorer window, right click on the component, folder or solution to export, and select Export. The first screen of the Export wizard, Select Context, is displayed.","Select whether to include components and dependencies from within the User Area by leaving the tickbox checked; or deselect the tickbox to include only components and dependencies from the Shared Area. ","If any of the components have labels assigned to them, you will have the option to include version labels with the Export job. To include version labels, check the tickbox and select the version labels to include. ","Click the arrow buttons to move single labels or all labels to the right hand window.","Click on the Next button to display the second screen of the Export wizard, View items. This screen displays the components and folders that will be included in the export job, in the context of their folder structures.","You must have at least read access for the components you are attempting to export. If you do not have read access, the export will be blocked at this point. Similarly, if you try to export a folder or component with unreadable dependencies, the export will be blocked at this point.","Click on the Next button to display the third screen of the wizard, Confirm selections. This screen inventories the components to be exported, along with their type, label, and revision number.","Click on the Next button to display the fourth screen of the wizard, Export job summary, to send the Export process to the Job Submission Console for remote execution. You can specify that the Job Submission Console will launch automatically when you exit the wizard.","Click on the Finish button to exit the wizard.","The Export job prioritises first by user domain (if ticked), then by labels (if selected and assigned to the exported component), then by shared area tip revision. The solution signature is included in the export. ","You can follow the progress of the Export job in the Job Submission Console. The details of the progress are logged in the job history, so you can easily diagnose any problems. When the job is complete, you can save the output job file for importing into a different solution.","Export a component, folder or solution","Exportacomponent,folderorsolution.htm");
Page[190]=new Array("The Export/Import functionality enables any user with read permission to export components, folders or entire solutions along with their dependencies.","The Export job creates an xml file that can be saved and used subsequently as input to an Import job.","To save an Export job file","In the Job Submission Console, right click on the Export job to display both the Export job xml file in the Output files window and the pop up menu:","Select Save to save the file to a specified location.","The xml file can now be imported from the saved location.","Save an Export job file","SaveanExportjobfile.htm");
Page[191]=new Array("The Export/Import functionality enables any user with read permission to export components, folders or entire solutions along with their dependencies. ","The user can import a previously exported component, folder or solution along with any dependent components and folder structures. The import process creates an Import job in the Job Submission Console. The imported file can only be imported at the solution level.","Only a user with the Solution Administrator or Architect functional role as part of their security profile will be able to create an Import job. ","The import functionality is also used to add pre-configured domains and solutions to a repository, as described in the Explorer overview.","To import a component, folder or solution","In the Explorer window, right click on the solution into which you want to import the component, folder or solution and select Import. ","If any component editors are open within the solution, a warning message is displayed. You will not be able to complete the import process if you are attempting to import a component that already exists and is open for editing.","The Import wizard is initiated. The first screen; Select import source, is displayed. Locate and select the xml file to import.","From the Files of type field, select Experian Proprietary Format: ","Click on the Next button to display the second screen of the Import wizard; View import file. Review the components and folder structure to be imported.","Click on the Next button to display the third screen of the Import wizard; Existing components. The screen will display a list of any components among those you are attempting to import that are already in the target solution. ","If you want to import the existing components, you must import them into your user area by checking the Import tickbox:","If you do not specify that the existing components are to be imported into your user area, they will not be imported.","If all the components already exist in the target solution, you will be unable to continue the import process until you check the tickbox; the following message will be displayed:","Click on the Next button to display the fourth screen of the Import wizard; Confirm choices. Review the name and the location of the imported file. ","Unless all components are to be imported into the user domain, the Comments field is mandatory; type a relevant comment. The comment is for users who want to know why a component was imported and it appears in the History of a component in the shared domain, in the Comments column.","The Label field is an optional field. ","Click on the Next button to display the fifth screen of the wizard; Import job summary.","The process will now be sent for remote execution. You can specify that the Job Submission Console will launch automatically when you exit the wizard by clicking in the Launch Job Submission Console tickbox.","You can follow the progress of the import job in the Job Submission Console. The details of the progress are logged in the job history, so you can easily diagnose any problems. When the job is complete, you will see the imported components and folders in the Explorer window under the appropriate solution. Unless otherwise specified, components are imported to the shared domain. The solution signature is included with the import.","The import job resolves all references automatically. If multiple import jobs are imported to the same solution, duplicate components and folders are resolved automatically (i.e., only a single instance of the component or folder will appear in the the target solution). ","Component names are case insensitive for import purposes; for example, the component &quot;Adverse Reason Code&quot; will be replaced by the imported component &quot;Adverse reason code&quot;.","Any missing folders are automatically created with the appropriate full list of allowed types. If a folder already exists, only the required allowed type will be added if missing and required for the purpose of the import. Any folders which are automatically created have all the associated publishing rules configured for that folder (in all directions). ","Import a component, folder or solution","Importacomponent,folderorsolution.htm");
Page[192]=new Array("The Import wizard is used to import a variety of file types into the software, depending on the context in which it has been activated.","Refer to the appropriate help topic from the following list:","Add a pre-configured domain","Add a pre-configured solution","Import a component, folder or solution","Import PMML data into a folder","Import SMG3 components using SDS v.1 solution structure","Import SMG3 components using SDS v.2.2 solution structure","Import Value Setter from csv file","Import wizard overview","Importwizardoverview.htm");
Page[193]=new Array("When integrating Strategy Design Studio with Transact it is important that Transact owns the data used within the Strategy Design Studio strategy; therefore, any changes required to the data should be made in Transact and imported into Strategy Design Studio using the Transact Data Definition Export Format import option within the import wizard. ","When Logical Data Sources and Physical Data Models are re-imported from Transact using the overwrite option, existing Logical Data Sources and Physical Data Models will be overwritten and any changes made in the Strategy Design Studio system will be lost. Characteristic references to components within the Strategy Design Studio system will be maintained with the imported data sources.","To import transact data into Strategy Design Studio","In the Explorer window, right click on the folder into which you want to import the Transact data. ","The Import wizard is initiated. The first screen, Select import source, is displayed. Locate and select the xml file to import.","From the Files of type field, select Transact Data Definition Export Format. ","Click on the Next button to display the second screen of the Import wizard, Select components to import. ","The wizard indicates by a check mark the components and component libraries that can be consumed into the Strategy Definition folder.","Components that can be imported into this folder (allowed component types) are identified by a check mark @. ","Components that are not allowed types are identified by @. ","For a first time import of data, the Overwrite existing object column is not relevant, and all entries are @.","To exclude any component from the import, click on the check mark @ and change it to an @.","Click on the Next button to display the third screen of the Import wizard, Confirm choices. Review the name and the location of the imported file.","Click on the Next button to display the fourth screen of the wizard, Import job summary.","Click on the Finish button to import the Transact data.","The import monitor is displayed on the bottom right of the screen:","To cancel the import process, click on the cancel button @ and click on the Yes button at the prompt.","When the import is finished, the Import complete message is displayed.","Transact Integration with Strategy Design Studio","TransactIntegrationwithStrategyDesignStudio.htm");
Page[194]=new Array("Label Management allows the user to define and tag a set of components that can then be acted upon as a group rather than individually. The label can be used to access the component set from the shared repository for export, check out, printing, deployment, etc. It is also used for versioning, to stamp a label onto a set of components or revisions to record the fact that they have been subjected to a specific action. Labels can be deployed repeatedly; different deployments are treated as different editions of the original label.","Labels can be assigned from the Explorer, or whenever a check-in action is performed on a component. The user can either create a new label or use an existing label (thus adding the component to an existing set). Labels can also be used when components are imported into a shared repository, to tag the set of components brought into the system. Labels themselves are stored in a shared area, available to all users.","Finally, the user can use labelling to pull together a component set by selecting individual components from the explorer; by assigning a label to a group of related components at the folder or solution level; or by some automatic discovery process (for example, all components referenced by a particular process flow).","While one label can be assigned to many different components, the same label cannot be assigned to different revisions of the same component. This is because labelling is intended to keep track of the various revisions in a coherent system. ","Label Management overview","LabelManagementoverview.htm");
Page[195]=new Array("The Label Management editor manages default labels and edition labels within a solution. From this editor, the user can create new labels, edit and delete labels, and display the label inventory; the user can also check out a labeled set of components, merge multiple sets of components under a single label, deploy a labeled set of components (as long as one of the components is deployable), and sanction or reject the pending deployment of a label. ","A label that has been successfully deployed (i.e., sanctioned) creates an edition of the original label; it is identified in the editor by the @ icon. Label editions are also identified by the label suffix applied when the label is deployed.","To open the editor, select Label Management from the Window menu in the Main menu bar of the user interface.","The Label Management editor consists of:","Label Management editor tool bar with options enabling the user to add, delete and edit labels, as well as to display the Label Inventory and to apply a filter to narrow the list of labels in the editor.","Label - label name","Status - deployment status (related to editions only):","Pending","Sanctioned","Rejected","Creation date - date the label was created","Author - who created the label","Update date - date the label was last updated","Update author - who last updated the label","Number of Components - number of components included under this label","Notes - notes included with the label (hover cursor over the notes icon to display the notes)","Adding an empty label to the editor","Click the Create label button @ on the tool bar to display the Create label dialog. Provide a label name and (optional) notes. The empty label is added to editor, and to the shared repository; it can be selected when checking in components, for example.","Deleting a label from the editor","Select a label and click the Delete label button @ on the tool bar to delete the label. This icon is greyed out for editions.","Editing a label","Select a label and click the Edit label button @ to display the Edit label dialog. The dialog allows the user to edit the name of the label, and to edit or add notes. This icon is greyed out for editions.","Viewing components","Click the View components button @ to display the Label Inventory.","Using the label filter","Click on the Show filter bar button @ to display the filter bar at the bottom of the editor: @ . The user can limit the number of labels displayed in the editor by typing letters into the content-sensitive filter. For example, typing in the letter &quot;B&quot; will limit the display to those labels whose names begin with B.","Label Management editor","LabelManagementeditor.htm");
Page[196]=new Array("The Label Management editor tool bar enables the user to add, delete and edit labels, as well as to display the Label Inventory and to apply a filter to narrow the list of labels.","@ Create label - create a new (empty) label","@ Delete label - delete an existing label. This icon is greyed out for editions.","@ Edit label - edit an existing label (name and notes only). This icon is greyed out for editions.","@ View components - view the contents and properties of a label in the Label Inventory window","@ Show/hide filter bar - filter the list of labels (filters by name)","Label Management editor tool bar","LabelManagementeditortoolbar.htm");
Page[197]=new Array("The Create label dialog allows the user to create a label name and (optional) notes for the label. ","For more information see Label Management editor","Create Label dialog","CreateLabeldialog.htm");
Page[198]=new Array("The Edit label dialog allows the user to edit the name of the label, and to edit or add notes.","For more information see Label Management editor","Edit Label dialog","EditLabeldialog.htm");
Page[199]=new Array("The user can select an individual component from the Explorer and assign a label to it; or the user can assign a label to all or some of the components within a selected folder or solution. ","The assigned label can be created as part of this process, or it can be a pre-existing label that may or may not include other components. The selected component can be added to the label by itself, or along with some or all of its dependent components. These various options are all managed by the Assign label wizard.  ","A label can also be assigned whenever a check-in action is performed on a component.","To assign a label to a component","From the Explorer window right click on a component and choose Assign label. The first screen of the Assign label wizard, Component Chooser, is displayed:","Select whether to; include only a custom selection of dependencies with the component by checking the tickbox or leave the tickbox unchecked to include all dependent components in the label. (The Select All and Unselect All buttons are not relevant in this set of instructions, as only one component has been selected for assignment.)","If more than one revision of this component exists, you can select the revision number to which you want to apply the label from the drop down list in the Revision column.","Continue at step 4 below.","To assign a label to a folder or solution","From the Explorer window right click on a folder or a solution and choose Manage components, then select Assign label. The first screen of the Assign label wizard, Component Chooser, is displayed:","Select whether to; include only a custom selection of dependencies with the component by checking the tickbox or leave the tickbox unchecked to include all dependent components in the label.","If more than one revision of any component exists, you can select the revision number to which you want to apply the label from the drop down list in the Revision column.","Click on the Next button. If the Custom selection tickbox has been left unchecked, the wizard skips to the third screen. If the tickbox has been checked, clicking on the Next button displays the second screen of the wizard, Custom selection of dependencies:","By default, all dependent components are selected to be included in the label along with the original component(s). Unselect the components you do not want to include in the label, or click on the @ button to include none of the dependent components. Click on  the @ button to display the Revision information.  ","Click on the Next button to display the third screen of the wizard, Label Chooser. A list of all labels in the solution is displayed:","At the bottom of the screen is a set of buttons that allow you to limit the display of labels to those that you have created, to display labels created recently, to create a new label or to display a list of components assigned to a label:","@ All labels - display the list of all labels in the solution","@ My labels - display only the labels you have created or modified","@ Recently changed - display labels that were changed in the past 7 days","@ Create label - create a new label for this component","@ Show label - display all components that are assigned the selected label: ","Select a label to assign or create a new label for the component(s).","It is not possible to select multiple labels.","Click on the Next button to display the fourth screen of the wizard; Summary. This displays information about the label you are creating and the list of components to which you are assigning the label. If the information displayed is correct, click on the Finish button to create the label.","The label has now been assigned to the selected component, folder or solution.","Assign a label to a component, folder or solution","Assignalabeltoacomponent,folderorsolution_1.htm");
Page[200]=new Array("The Label Chooser dialog allow you to select a label from a list of all the available labels in the solution.","For more information see Assign a label to a component","Label Chooser dialog","LabelChooserdialog.htm");
Page[201]=new Array("Labels can be unassigned to components from the Label Inventory.","An Edition label cannot be unassigned.","To unassign a label","Open the Label Inventory from the Label Management editor or from the Label Chooser screen of any of the label wizards, by selecting a label and clicking the View components button @.","Click on the component for which you want to unassign the label, or select multiple labels by holding down the Ctrl key while selecting the labels, then right click on a label and select Unassign label from the menu.","At the prompt, click Yes to unassign the component(s).","The label(s) has been usassigned from the component(s).","Unassign a label to a component","Unassignalabeltoacomponent_1.htm");
Page[202]=new Array("The Label Management editor enables the user to check out a set of associated components by checking out the label assigned to them.","To check out a label","From the Window menu, select Label Management from the Window menu. The Label Management editor is displayed.","From the Label Management editor, select a label to check out.","Right click on the label and select Check-out from the menu. The first screen of the Check-out wizard, Component Chooser, is displayed:","The following information is displayed for each component:","Name - component name","@ Broken state - indicates if the component is in a broken state","@ Revision user area - displays component version number in the user domain","@ Revision shared area - displays component version number in the shared domain","Update date - displays the date component was last updated","Update author - displays who last updated the component","Status - displays if the component can be checked out","Detail - display label detail","Select - check the tickbox to include the component in the check out procedure","Select the components to check out. By default, all components are selected. If there are problems with any components, the Accept Warnings tickbox will become activated. You can still check out a problem component by checking the tickbox.","Click Next to display the second screen of the wizard, Summary. The Summary screen displays the list of components that will be checked out if you continue.","If you are satisfied with the list, click Finish to check out the set of components.","The set of components associated with the label are checked out.","Check out a label","Checkoutalabel.htm");
Page[203]=new Array("The Label Management editor enables the user to merge sets of associated components by merging the labels assigned to them.","To merge labels","From the Window menu, select Label Management from the Window menu. The Label Management editor is displayed.","From the Label Management editor, select the labels to merge. To select multiple labels, hold down the Ctrl key while clicking on a label.","Right click on one of the selected labels and select Merge from the menu. The first screen of the Merge Labels wizard, Component Chooser, is displayed:","By default, all components are selected to merge. Unselect any components you do not want to include in the merge.","Click Next to display the second screen of the wizard, Label Chooser. The list of all labels in the solution is displayed:","At the bottom of the screen is a set of buttons that allow you to narrow the display of labels; to create a new label; or to display a list of components assigned to a label:","@ All labels - display the list of all labels in the solution","@ My labels - display only the labels you created or modified","@ Recently changed - display labels that were changed in the past 7 days","@ Create label - create a new label for this merged set of components","@ Show label - display all components that are assigned the selected label: ","Select a label to assign or create a new label for the merged set of components.","Click Next to display the third screen of the wizard, Summary. This displays information about the label you are creating, and the list of components to which you are assigning the label. If the information displayed is correct, click Finish to create the label that includes the merged set of components.","The components from the selected labels have now been merged.","If the same component with the same revision exists in several labels to be merged, then this component and revision will appear once in the outcome label.","If the same component with different revisions exists in several labels to be merged, then the highest component revision will appear by default in the outcome label; one of the older revisions can be manually selected by the user.","Merge labels","Mergelabels.htm");
Page[204]=new Array("The Label Inventory displays the components assigned to a selected label. The inventory can be displayed from the Label Management editor or from the Label Chooser screen of any of the label wizards, by clicking the View components button @.","Components can be checked out from the inventory, and labels can be unassigned to a component.","By default, the inventory displays the following information for each component:","Name - component name","Type - component type","@ Revision shared area - displays component version number in the shared domain","Update date - displays the date component was last updated","Update author - displays who last updated the component","Click on the Change visible columns button @ to display and select other columns to display:","Using the label filter","Click on the Show filter bar button @ to display the filter bar at the bottom of the editor: @ . The user can limit the number of labels displayed in the editor by typing letters into the content-sensitive filter. For example, typing in the letter B will limit the display to those labels whose names begin with B.  ","Checking out a component","To check a component out from the Label Inventory, right click on the component and select Check-out. The Component Chooser screen of the Check-out wizard is displayed.","Label Inventory","LabelInventory.htm");
Page[205]=new Array("Labels are deployed from the Label Management editor. There are several deployable components; examples include:","Decision process flow","Call interface","Decision reason code table","Only one decision process flow can be deployed on one label; the same label may include 0, 1, or many call interfaces and/or decision reason codes.","Business Process Composition","Only one Business Process Composition can be deployed on one label.","Customer Management Solution","Only one Customer Management Solution can be deployed on one label.","Connectivity Process Flow  ","Only one Connectivity Process Flow can be deployed on one label.","In order to be able to Deploy a label the user must have Deploy privileges assigned.<br>For more information see the topic Edit or Configure Capability Permissions","Label deployment supports an embedded lifecycle status. When initially deployed, strategies (i.e., decision process flow deployments) are identified as Pending and can be distributed onto testing platforms outside the studio environment. The live runtime environment will only accept Sanctioned deployments.","The label deployment process is the same as the Deployment process that can be triggered from within the Batch Process Flow. The system used the same validation and deployment rules.","To deploy a label","Open the Label Management editor by selecting Label Management from the Window menu. ","Right click on the label to deploy, and select Deploy from the menu. To select more than one label, hold down the Ctrl key and click on the labels.","The Label Deployment dialog is displayed. ","Provide a Label Suffix, and click Apply to All to add the suffix to the Edition Name. You can also edit the Edition Name and Deployment Notes directly.","Provide notes for this deployment, if desired, and click Apply to All to add these notes to the Deployment Notes.","Check the tickbox to select the label to deploy, and click Deploy.","In the case of call interface and decision reason code table deployments, a new label edition is created and displayed in the Label Management editor with the status of Sanctioned @. ","In the case of all other deployments, a new label edition is created and displayed in the Label Management editor with the status of  Pending @. The pending label is now ready to be sanctioned or rejected. ","In either case, the original label remains and can be deployed again. The status of the deployment job can be further viewed in the Job Submission Console.","Using Batch Process Flow to create an XML of a deployed label","The user can create an XML of the deployed label, which is a snapshot of the system at the point of deployment. The user must run the deployment using a Batch Process Flow which contains a deployment job and an export job based on the specific label. ","When the Batch Process Flow  is submitted to the Job Submission Framework, it completes the deployment and produces the deployment files and the system export.xml file (the snapshot of the system). ","Note that the export file is always given the default name of export.xml, so if the user defines more than one export job in a single Batch Process Flow, the second export file will overwrite the first (even if they are based on different labels). ","See the Batch Process Flow help for details on the deployment process.","Deploy a label","Deployalabel.htm");
Page[206]=new Array("The Label Deployment dialog enables the user to deploy one or more labels at a time. The user can supply edition names and deployment notes.","The Label Deployment dialog consists of the following:","Label Suffix - enter a label suffix that can be applied to all deployed labels at once to provide a uniform edition name. Alternatively, an edition name can be typed directly into the Edition Name field.","Notes - enter notes that can be applied to all deployed labels at once. Alternatively, notes can be typed directly into the Deployment Notes field.","@ - click to apply the contents of the Label Suffix and/or Notes fields to all labels selected for deployment.","Select - select the labels to deploy.","Label Name - name of the label selected for deployment from the Label Management editor. Field is not editable.","Edition Name - name of the label edition as it will appear in the Label Management editor once it is deployed. Must be different from the Label Name.","Deployment Notes - optional notes regarding the deployment.","@ - select all labels for deployment.","@ - deselect all labels selected for deployment.","@ - deploy all selected labels.","@ - cancel the deployment and close the dialog.","Label Deployment dialog","LabelDeploymentdialog.htm");
Page[207]=new Array("When a label has been deployed initially, it is identified in the Label Management editor with the status of Pending @. At this point, it is ready to be Sanctioned or Rejected.","Deployed call interface and decision reason code table components do not need to be sanctioned; they are sanctioned automatically upon deployment.","In order to be able to Sanction or Reject a label the user must have Sanction privileges assigned.<br>For more information see the topic Edit or Configure Capability Permissions","To Sanction a Pending label","From the Label Management editor, right click on the pending label and select Sanction from the menu.","The Sanction Deployment editor  is displayed.","Supply any notes to be included with the action, and check the tickbox to select the label to sanction.","Click Sanction to deploy the label. The Status of the label deployment is changed to Sanctioned @.","The Job Reference number is listed in the Label Deployment Output window. The progress of the deployment job can be viewed in the Job Submission Console. ","The deployment job creates a deployment bundle .ser file, by default in the Job Server\\Work folder, under a subfolder identified by the job reference number. You can also save the file directly from Job Submission Console to a location of your choice (see Display and save output files)."," The deployment file can be passed on for implementation in the acceptance/production environments.","To Reject a Pending label","From the Label Management editor, right click on the pending label and select Reject from the menu.","The Reject Deployment editor  is displayed.","Supply any notes to be included with the action, and check the tickbox to select the label to reject.","Click Reject to reject the pending deployment. The Status of the label deployment is changed to Rejected @.","The pending job has been rejected and will not be deployed.","Sanction or Reject a deployed label","SanctionorRejectadeployedlabel.htm");
Page[208]=new Array("The Reject Deployment editor enables the user to reject the deployment of a pending label.","The Reject Deployment editor includes the following:","Notes - notes that can be applied to all labels being rejected. Alternatively, notes can be typed directly into the Reject Notes field.","@ - click to apply the notes to all rejected labels.","Select - select the labels to reject.","Label Name - name of the label selected from the  Label Management editor. Field can not be edited.","Reject Notes - notes regarding the rejection of the label.","Reject Deployment editor","RejectDeploymenteditor.htm");
Page[209]=new Array("The Sanction Deployment editor enables the user to sanction the deployment of a pending label.","The Sanction Deployment editor includes the following:","Notes - notes that can be applied to all labels being sanctioned. Alternatively, notes can be typed directly into the Sanction Notes field.","@ - click to apply the notes to all sanctioned labels.","Select - select the labels to sanction.","Label Name - name of the label selected from the  Label Management editor. Field can not be edited.","Sanction Notes - notes regarding the sanctioning of the label.","Sanction Deployment editor","SanctionDeploymenteditor.htm");
Page[210]=new Array("A printable document can be invoked for view or for print out from the Explorer window and from the Main menu bar of the user interface. Only components that the user has access to will be available to view as a printable document.","From the Explorer window there are three different types of printable documents available, printable documents are available at the Solution, Folder and Component level:","Inventory: When Print &gt; Inventory is selected the printable document will contain a list of the names of the components contained in the solution,  folder or component from which the user invoked Print. See the Produce an Inventory printable document help topic for more detail.","Summary: When Print &gt; Summary is selected the printable document will contain a list of the name of the component(s) contained in the solution, folder or component from which the user has invoked print as well as a printout of the component itself. Using a scorecard as an example, if the user selects Print &gt; Summary, the printable document will include the name and inventory details of the scorecard in addition to a printable document of the scorecard itself. See the Produce a Summary printable document help topic for more detail.","Detailed: When Print &gt; Details is selected the printable document will containing the name of the component(s) contained in the solution, folder or component from which the user has invoked print, a printable document of the component itself as well the names and properties of all the dependent components. Using a scorecard as the example, the printable document will be the same as the summary, but will also include details of the referenced and embedded class sets, matrices and boolean expressions as well as all the characteristics and logical data sources they reference. See the Produce a Detailed printable document help topic for more detail.","The Main menu bar of the user interface allows the user to set one type to be made available for view and print. The Lite print can be made available here, it is not available for selection from the Explorer window.","The Lite level must be selected in the Printing dialog available in Options. Please see the  Produce a Lite printable document help topic for more information.","Lite: When File&gt;Printable Lite Doc is selected the printable document will contain a view of the component the user has open in the editor. The printout will not include a front page.","When the print type has been selected the Print editor will be displayed in the Main editor. It is from this editor that the actual printout can be manipulated.","Printing overview","Printingoverview.htm");
Page[211]=new Array("When printing is initiated, the Print editor is initiated in the Main editor area of the user interface. The editor displays a preview of the selected printable document.","The Print editor consists of:","Print editor tool bar - tool bar with options designed to assist the user in manipulating the printout.<br>Print Preview area - this shows the user what the output will look like when it is printed or saved.","The Print editor allows the user to select and configure:","The printing output type (PDF, MS Office, HTML document or a physical printer)","The printing destination (for PDF, MS Office and HTML document output)","Print editor","PrintPreviewdialog.htm");
Page[212]=new Array("The Print editor tool bar is situated in the Print editor and contains buttons for saving and printing, for zooming and for navigation inside the document.","@  Save - Saves the output document on the hard drive","@  Print - Prints a hard copy of the output document","@  First Page - Navigates to the first page","@  Previous Page - Navigates to the previous page","@  Next Page - Navigates to the next page","@   Last Page - Navigates to the last page","@  Go to page - Navigates to a chosen page number","@   Actual Size - Zooms the document to its actual size","@   Fit Page - Zooms the document to fit in the preview area","@  Fit Width - Zooms the document to fit the width of the preview area","@   Zoom In - Zooms in the document to the next incremental value (e.g. 50%, 75%, etc.)","@   Zoom Out - Zooms out the document to the next incremental value (e.g. 50%, 75%, etc.)","@   Zoom Ratio - drop down list allows the user to choose a specific size of the preview","Print editor tool bar","Printeditortoolbar.htm");
Page[213]=new Array("There are four different types of printable documents available:","Inventory:  An Inventory printable document containing the selected component; giving the Component type, Component name, Shared revision, User revision, Modified status, Update date and time and the Last author.","Summary: A Summary printable document containing the selected component; giving Component name, Shared revision, User revision, Type, Modified status, Updated date and time and the Last author. The printable document will also contain details of the selected component&#8217;s contents.","Detailed: A Detailed printable document containing the selected component, giving Component name, Shared revision, User revision, Type, Modified status, Updated date and time and the Last author. The printable document will also contain details of the selected component&#8217;s contents. It will also include details of the referenced and embedded content.","Lite: A Lite printable document containing the component that the user has open in the editor, giving the same detail as the Summary printable document. There is no front page.<br>Not all components support Lite printing.","Print Levels","PrintLevels.htm");
Page[214]=new Array("An Inventory printable document containing the selected component; giving the Component type, Component name, Shared revision, User revision, Modified status, Update date and time and the Last author.","To produce an Inventory printable document","Right click on a solution, folder or component in the Explorer window and select Printable Doc, then select Inventory.","The print editor will be displayed in the Main editor area of the user interface.","To save the printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Save dialog.","Locate the folder to which you would like this printable document to be saved and click on the Save button.","To print the Inventory printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Print Dialog for your printer.","Configure the printable document as appropriate for your requirements.","Produce an Inventory printable document","ProduceanInventoryprintabledocument.htm");
Page[215]=new Array("A Summary printable document containing the selected component; giving Component name, Shared revision, User revision, Type, Modified status, Updated date and time and the Last author. The printable document will also contain details of the selected component&#8217;s contents.","To produce a Summary printable document","Right click on a solution, folder or component in the Explorer window and select Printable Doc, then select Summary.","The print editor will be displayed in the Main editor area of the user interface.","To save the Summary printout, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Save dialog.","Locate the folder to which you would like this printout to be saved and click on the Save button.","To print the Summary printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Print dialog for your printer.","Configure the printout as appropriate for your requirements.","Produce a Summary printable document","ProduceaSummaryprintabledocument.htm");
Page[216]=new Array("A Detailed printable document containing the selected component, giving Component name, Shared revision, User revision, Type, Modified status, Updated date and time and the Last author. The printable document will also contain details of the selected component&#8217;s contents. It will also include details of the referenced and embedded content.","To produce a Detailed printable document","Right click on a solution, folder or component in the Explorer window and select Printable Doc, then select Detailed.","The print editor will be displayed in the Main editor area of the user interface.","To save the printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Save dialog.","Locate the folder to which you would like this printable document to be saved and click on the Save button.","To print the Detailed printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Print Dialog for your printer.","Configure the printable document as appropriate for your requirements.","Produce a Detailed printable document","ProduceaDetailedprintabledocument.htm");
Page[217]=new Array("A Lite print will produce a printable document of the component the user has open in the editor. The printable document will not include a front page.","The Lite level must be selected in the Printing dialog available in Options.","To select the Lite print option","In the Main menu bar of the user interface, click on Tools.","Select Options.","The Options dialog will be initiated.","Click on the @ icon.","Click on the General tab.","In the Level field of the Options dialog, tick the lite tick box to select.","Click on the OK button.","The lite print option has now been selected. You may now produce a lite printable document.","To produce a lite printable document","Highlight the required component in the Explorer window."," In the Main menu bar of the user interface, click on File.","Select Printable Lite Doc.","The print editor will be displayed in the Main editor area of the user interface.","To save the lite printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Save dialog.","Locate the folder to which you would like this printout to be saved and click on the Save button.","To print the lite print, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Print dialog for your printer.","Configure the printout as appropriate for your requirements.","Produce a Lite printable document","ProduceaLiteprintabledocument.htm");
Page[218]=new Array("The user can produce an Inventory, Summary or Detailed printable document from the software. A printable document can be saved to a location of the users choice, in either PDF, RTF or HTML format in order that it can be printed or used when required.","To save a printable document","Right click on a solution, folder or component in the Explorer window and choose Printable Doc, then select Inventory, Summary or Detailed.","To save the printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.","The system will open the Save dialog.","Locate the folder to which you would like this printable document to be saved and the format of the save.","Click on the Save button.","The printable document will be saved to the location you have chosen and be available to print as required.","The user may also Produce a Lite printable document and save this if required.","Save a printable document","Saveaprintabledocument.htm");
Page[219]=new Array("The user can produce an Inventory, Summary or Detailed printable document from the software.","To print a printable document","Right click on a solution, folder or component in the Explorer window and select Printable Doc, then select Inventory, Summary or Detailed.","The print editor will be displayed in the Main editor area of the user interface.","To print the printable document, click on the @ icon in the print editor tool bar.<br>","The system will open the Print dialog for your printer.","Configure the printable document as appropriate for your requirements.","Click on the OK button.","The document will now be printed.","The user may also Produce a Lite printable document and print this if required.","Print a printable document","Printaprintabledocument.htm");
Page[220]=new Array("Print Themes allow custom configuration of the sequence in which components will appear at the start and end of a printable document, the rules apply to all print types and each section of the printable document (inventory view, individual component order and embedded components).","The user can select a Print Theme in the Printing dialog available in Options.","Only custom themes configured for the studio that the user is running will be available for selection. There is a one standard default theme available for all product studios. Availability of any additional themes is dependent on whether the individual studio product capabilities installed include any additional themes.","Print Themes","PrintThemes.htm");
Page[221]=new Array("The user can select a Print Theme in the Printing dialog available in Options.","Only custom themes that have been configured for the studio that a user is running will be available for selection.","To select a Print Theme","In the Main menu bar of the user interface, click on Tools.","Select Options.","The Options dialog will be initiated.","Click on the @ icon.","Click on the Component Sequence tab.","In the Profile field, select the appropriate theme from the drop down list.","A text pane will be displayed giving information about the theme you have chosen.","Click on the OK button.","The Print Theme is now set.","The user can produce an Inventory, Summary, Detailed or Lite printable document from the software.","Select a Print Theme","SelectaPrintTheme.htm");
Page[222]=new Array("The publishing mechanism allows for the sharing of components between folders within a Solution boundary &#8211; for example definitions of data models and layouts can be located in a folder and published for use within other parts of the Solution &#8211; but not within other Solutions. ","Without the publishing capability the user would need to re-create the components in multiple folders, duplicating effort and components in order to use the definitions throughout the Solution.","The publishing mechanism is activated from any folder in the Explorer window. It is this folder that is known as the 'source' folder and contains the components that will be published to other folders. The mode chosen (Outbound/Inbound) will determine how the folders are displayed. When the Outbound mode is selected the editor will display the folders to which the content of the source file has been published. When the Inbound mode is selected the editor will display those folders whose contents have been published to the source folder.","Publishing can be carried out in two forms:","Direct","Hierarchical","Direct publishing is illustrated in the editor by a blue folder, either @ or @. This shows that publishing has been carried out between folders.","Hierarchical publishing is illustrated in the editor by a green folder, either @ or @. This shows that publishing has been carried out between parent and child folders. If a child folder or parent folder is added where hierarchical publishing has already been carried out, the hierarchical publishing will automatically be applied to the new folder. ","Folder A contains a logical data source that contains generic application characteristics, folder B will be where the scorecards are created and folder C where the segmentation rules will be created. ","By publishing from the source folder, (folder A) to folder B and C, the scorecards and segmentation rules can be built using the characteristics defined in folder A. ","Publishing folder B to folder C enables the segmentation rules to be used to define the scorecard. ","Any amendments made to the original component will automatically be updated to the published instances of the component throughout the solution without the user needing to carry out any further action.","The publishing mechanism will only be available to those users who have the appropriate access rights. ","When Publish is selected from the Explorer window the Publishing editor is opened along with the Publishing Inventory window.","@ ","Publishing Editor - enables the user to define specifically which folders to publish to and provides a graphical representation of the current publishing rules for the folder that is selected. ","Publishing Inventory window - provides a summary of the publishing rules that have been carried out throughout the whole system.","Publishing overview","Publishingoverview.htm");
Page[223]=new Array("The Publishing editor enables the user to define specifically which folders to publish to, and provides a graphical representation of the current publishing rules for the folder that is selected.","The publishing editor consists:","Publishing editor tool bar with options designed to assist the user in defining the publishing rules.","Publishing Editor - displays, using coloured folders, what publishing rules are currently in existence for the source folder. ","@  Source Folder - Outbound - any blue (direct) or green (hierarchical) folders displayed in the editor contain the contents published from this folder.","@  Source Folder - Inbound - any blue (direct) or green (hierarchical) folders displayed in the editor have had their contents published to the source folder.","@ Direct - the content of the source folder has been directly published to this folder. ","@ Hierarchical - the content of the source folder has been hierarchically published to this folder.","Using the Publishing editor the contents of the source folder can be published directly to other folders or hierarchically to parent or child folders. ","Publishing Inventory window - enables the user to see an inventory view of all publishing rules that have been carried out in the solution. The list will alter depending on whether Outbound or Inbound has been selected in the Publishing editor.","Publishing editor","Publishingeditor.htm");
Page[224]=new Array("The Publishing editor tool bar is located across the top of the Publishing editor and is designed to assist the user in defining the publishing rules.","@ Outbound - will display all folders that have content that has been published from the Source folder, see  Outbound/inbound publishing examples","@ Inbound - will display all the folders that have published their content to the Source folder, see  Outbound/inbound publishing examples","@ Zoom in and Zoom out - select to enlarge or reduce the size of the image seen in the editor","@ Zoom To Fit - resizes the image to fit the editor the user has open","@ Zoom Reset - resizes the image back to how it was displayed when the editor was first opened","@ Align Middle - will align all objects using the horizontal middle point for alignment","@ Align Vertical - will align all objects vertical middle point for alignment","@   Display source and target(s) folders only - if outbound is selected, selecting this icon will display in the editor those folders that have content that has been published from the Source folder. If inbound is selected, selecting this icon will display all the folders that have published their content to the Source folder.","@ Check impact of current rule changes - ensures that the publishing rules that have been defined are valid","@ Apply current folder's rules changes - select to apply the amended publishing rules to the folder","@ Remove all rules for current Source Folder - select to delete all the publishing rules that have been defined for the source folder that is currently selected","Publishing editor tool bar","Publishingeditortoolbar.htm");
Page[225]=new Array("The following two diagrams illustrate how differently the publishing rules for a folder can be displayed in the Physical Data Model editor when Outbound and Inbound are selected.","<br>@ Illustrates that the contents of the Data Universe have been published directly to the Scorecards and Decision Process Flow and hierarchically to Credit Cards and ACME Lending folders.","<br>@ Illustrates that the contents of the Derived Data and Data Universe folders have been published directly into the Scorecards folder.","Outbound/inbound publishing examples","inboundpublishingexamples.htm");
Page[226]=new Array("The Publishing Inventory window enables the user to see an inventory view of all publishing rules that have been carried out in the solution. The list will alter depending on whether Outbound or Inbound has been selected in the Publishing editor.","The Publishing Inventory window consists of the Publishing Inventory window tool bar, the Inventory table and the Filter.","Publishing Inventory window tool bar - The Publishing Inventory window tool bar is displayed down the left hand side of the window and selecting options from this tool bar alters the content of the inventory.","The Inventory table consists of up to 4 columns. To add or remove a column, right click in the column header row and the Change Visible columns dialog will be initiated. Simply tick to display or un tick to remove. The Change Visible Columns dialog can also be initiated by clicking on the @ icon in the Publishing Inventory window.","Available columns are;","Source - displays the name of the source folder used to create the publishing rule","Path -  displays the entire path of the source folder used to create the publishing rule","Type - indicates the type of publishing rule (transversal / hierarchical up or down)","Target - displays the name of the target folder used to create the publishing rule","Filter - Typing entries into the Filter box will filter out the names of target folders that do not match the contents of the filter. Select the Clear button to remove the filter selection.","Publishing Inventory window","PublishingInventorywindow.htm");
Page[227]=new Array("The Publishing Inventory window tool bar is displayed down the left hand side of the Publishing Inventory window and enables the user to alter the content of the displayed inventory.","@Expand All - expands the contents of all the folders to display fully all the outbound or inbound publishing rules that exist in the solution","@ Collapse All - collapses the list so that only the folders are displayed ","@  Switch from Target to Source grouping - will cause the inventory window to display either Outbound publishing rules or Inbound publishing rules","@   Display current folder's rules only - when displayed the rules for all folders are displayed","Publishing Inventory window tool bar","PublishingInventorywindowtoolbar.htm");
Page[228]=new Array("The publishing mechanism allows for the sharing of components between folders within the Solution boundary, but not within other Solutions. The publishing mechanism is activated from any folder in the Explorer window. It is this folder that is known as the 'source' folder and contains the components that will be published to other folders.","To change which folder is the source file","With the Publishing editor open, locate the folder which you wish to change to be the source file.","Double click on this folder.<br>@<br>If any publishing rules have been modified the system will display a confirmation dialog, asking if you would like the rules applied.","Click on the Yes button to apply the changes, click on the No button to discard the changes.<br>The folder will change to become the source folder.","The colours of the folders displayed in the editor will change to reflect the change.","Change which folder is the source file","Changewhichfolderisthesourcefile.htm");
Page[229]=new Array("The publishing mechanism allows for the sharing of components between folders within the Solution boundary, but not within other Solutions. The publishing mechanism is activated from any folder in the Explorer window. It is this folder that is known as the 'source' folder and contains the components that will be published to other folders.","To publish to parent  or child folders","In the Explorer window, right-click on the folder that you wish to publish and Select Publish.<br>The system will open the Publishing editor with the source folder highlighted as follows:<br>@<br>The Publishing Inventory window for the whole solution will also be open.","Ensure that the @ option in the tool bar is selected.","Click on the source folder.<br>@","Depending on the structure of your system either one or two green arrows will be displayed.","Select the &quot;up&quot; arrow to publish to all the parent folders of the source folder or select the &quot;down&quot; arrow to publish to all the child folders of the source folder.","Continue publishing to the folders you require.","Click the @ icon to check the validity of the publishing rules you have made.","Click the @ icon to apply these rules to the solution.","The publishing rules and Publishing Inventory window will be updated.","Publish to parent or child folders","Publishtoparentorchildfolders.htm");
Page[230]=new Array("All the publishing rules can be removed for a selected source folder.","To remove the rules for a source folder","In the Explorer window, right-click on the folder whose rules you wish to amend and select Publish.","Click on the @ icon.","The system will display a confirmation dialog.","Click on the Yes button.","All the publishing rules for the currently selected source folder will be deleted.","Remove the rules for a source folder","Removetherulesforasourcefolder.htm");
Page[231]=new Array("The publishing mechanism allows for the sharing of components between folders within the Solution boundary, but not within other Solutions. The publishing mechanism is activated from any folder in the Explorer window. It is this folder that is known as the 'source' folder and contains the components that will be published to other folders.","To remove/unpublish the rules from a selected folder","In the Explorer window, select the mode you require, either Outbound or Inbound from the Publishing editor tool bar.","Right-click on the folder whose contents you wish to remove and select Unpublish.<br>The rules for this folder for the mode you have selected will be removed.","Click the @ icon to check the validity of the publishing rules you have made.","Click the @ icon to apply these rules to the solution.","The publishing rules and Publishing Inventory window will be updated.","Remove/Unpublish the rules from a selected folder","Unpublishtherulesfromaselectedfolder.htm");
Page[232]=new Array("The publishing mechanism allows for the sharing of components between folders within the Solution boundary, but not within other Solutions. The publishing mechanism is activated from any folder in the Explorer window. It is this folder that is known as the 'source' folder and contains the components that will be published to other folders.","To publish to another folder","In the Explorer window, right-click on the folder that you wish to publish and Select Publish.<br>The system will open the Publishing editor with the source folder highlighted as follows:<br>@","Double clicking on a &quot;normal&quot; folder will alter the state of the folder to being the source folder. ","The Publishing Inventory window for the whole solution will also be open.","Ensure that the @ option in the tool bar is selected.","Click on the folder where you wish the contents of the source folder to be published. A blue arrow will be displayed with a tool tip confirming to you where the publishing is going to take place.<br>@  ","Click on the blue arrow. The folder will change to illustrate that the contents of the source folder have been published to this folder.<br>@","Continue publishing to the folders you require.","Click the @ icon to check the validity of the publishing rules you have made.","Click the @ icon to apply these rules to the solution.","The publishing rules and Publishing Inventory window will be updated.","Publish directly to another folder","Publishdirectlytoanotherfolder.htm");
Page[233]=new Array("The publishing mechanism allows for the sharing of components between folders within the Solution boundary, but not within other Solutions. The publishing mechanism is activated from any folder in the Explorer window. It is this folder that is known as the 'source' folder and contains the components that will be published to other folders.","To copy the published contents from one folder to another folder","In the Publishing editor, select the mode you require, either Outbound or Inbound from the Publishing editor tool bar.","Right click on the folder whose contents you wish to copy and select Copy.<br>@<br>@","Right click on the folder where you wish the rules to be published and select Paste.","Depending on the mode you have selected either the outbound publishing rules or the inbound publishing rules will be pasted into the folder you have selected.","Click on the @ icon to check the validity of the publishing rules you have made.","Click on the @ icon to apply these rules to the solution.","The publishing rules and Publishing Inventory window will be updated.","Copy the published contents of a folder into another folder","Copythepublishedcontentsofafolderintoanotherfolder.htm");
Page[234]=new Array("The Advanced Search function allows the user to search component details for the following;","Words, Phrases, Dates, Users, Component types and Component states.","Advanced Search can be initiated form the Main menu bar and has a basic and an advanced option. The function can also be activated by using Ctrl+Shift+F.","The basic search can be defined to search for a word or phrase. The search can be defined as the whole word or to match the case. The search scope can be defined to search within all open solutions or the current solution only.","There is also the option to carry out a more advanced search.","The Advanced Search can be defined in a further four ways: by Dates, by Users, by Component type and by Other (which includes broken, hidden, conflict and locally modified).","Any returned search results from an Advanced Search (basic and advanced) will be returned and displayed in the Search Results window located in the Output area of the user interface.","The Quick Search function is also available to the user.","Advanced Search overview","AdvancedSearchoverview.htm");
Page[235]=new Array("The Advanced Search function allows the user to search component details for the following;","Words, Phrases, Dates, Users, Component types and Component states.","Advanced Search can be initiated form the Main menu bar and has a basic and an advanced option.","Any returned search results from an Advanced Search (basic or advanced) will be returned and displayed in the Search window located in the Output area of the user interface.","The user can perform some actions by right clicking on a component row in the window. The actions available depend upon the component type. Available actions are the same as the actions available in the Explorer window; please see the Explorer window help page for further information. Double clicking on a component in the Component column will open the component in the Main editor.","The user can customize this window:","A  user can change the column order by clicking on a column header and dragging into the preferred place. ","@ Filter: Use this button to display or remove the Filter bar at the bottom of the window. The user can use the filter field to filter for specific words.","@ Change visible columns: Use this button to choose which column to view. The user can remove or add columns from view using the Change Visible Columns button.This is only visible in the window when the Filter field is visible. This is also available on right click in the column header.","The following columns are available:","Component: This column displays the Component name.  ","@ Area state: This column displays the domain that the component sits in.  @ indicates that the component sits in a user domain.  @ indicates that the component sits in a shared domain.","Author: This column displays the author/creator of the component.","@ Broken state: This column displays the broken state of a component. @ indicates that there are no publishing rules defined between the component and a dependant component. If the field is empty, the component is not broken.","@ Component state: This column displays the component state.  @ indicates a new component.  @ indicates a modified component. If the field is empty, the component is unmodified.  ","@ Conflict state: This column displays the conflict state of the component. @ indicates that there is a conflict. If the field is empty, there is no conflict.    ","Creation date: This column displays the date the Component was created. ","@ Favourite state: This column displays any components that the user has marked as a favourite.","@ Lock state: This column displays the Lock/Unlock status of the component. @  indicates that the component is locked. If the field is empty, the component is not locked. ","Locked by: This column displays the user name of the user currently locking the component.","Name: This column displays the Name that has been given to the component.","Path: This column allows the user to display the full path of a component.","@ Revision shared area: This column displays the version number of the component on the shared domain.","@ Revision user area: This column displays the version number of the component on the user domain.","Type: This column displays the Component Type (Decision Process Flow, Call Interface Manager, etc.)","Update Author: This column displays the author responsible for the latest update of the component.","Update date: This column displays the last date that the component was updated.","Advanced Search results","AdvancedSearchresults.htm");
Page[236]=new Array("The basic Search Window dialog allows the user to search for a word or a phrase. The basic search can be defined to search for the whole word or to match the case. The search scope can be defined to search within all open solutions or the current solution only.","Please see the Use Basic Advanced Search help topic for information on how to proceed.","Search Window dialog - Basic","SearchWindowdialog-Basic.htm");
Page[237]=new Array("The advanced Search Window dialog allows the user to search for a word or a phrase. The Advanced Search can be defined in a further four ways: by Dates, by Users, by Component type and by Other (which includes broken, hidden, conflict and locally modified).","Please see the Use Advanced Search help topic for information on how to proceed.","Search Window dialog - Advanced","SearchWindowdialog-Advanced.htm");
Page[238]=new Array("The Advanced Search function allows the user to search component details for the following;","Words, Phrases, Dates, Users, Component types and Component states.","Advanced Search can be initiated from the Main menu bar and has a basic and an advanced option.","The Advanced Search function (basic and advanced) enables the user to search component detail in solutions only.","To search for a word or phrase using Basic Advanced Search","Load a solution. ","You will be unable to carry out a search until you have loaded a solution.","Click on Edit in the Main menu bar and select Advanced Search.","The Search Window dialog will be displayed.","Type a name or word in the Name text field.","To define a search on the whole word or a search to match case, ensure that the appropriate tick box is selected.","To define the search scope, ensure that either the Open Solutions or the Current Solution tick box is selected.","You may continue to a further Advanced Search by clicking on the Advanced... button in the Search Window dialog.","Click on the Find button.","The search results will be displayed in the Search Results window, located in the output area of the user interface. ","Use Basic Advanced Search","UseBasicAdvancedSearch.htm");
Page[239]=new Array("The Advanced Search function allows the user to search components details for the following;","Words, Phrases, Dates, Users, Component types and Component states.","Advanced Search can be initiated form the Main menu bar and has a basic and an advanced option.","The Advanced Search function (basic and advanced) enables the user to search for components in solutions only.","To search for a word or phrase using the Advanced Search","Load a solution. ","You will be unable to carry out a search until you have loaded a solution.","Steps 4 to 6 are not mandatory. You can directly switch to the advanced mode at step 7 and enter the detail in the Advance Search Window dialog. ","Click on Edit in the Main menu bar and select Advanced Search.","The Search Window dialog will be displayed.","Type a name or word in the Name text field.","To define a search on the whole word or a search to match case, ensure that the appropriate tick box is selected.","To define the search scope, ensure that either the Open Solutions or the Current Solution tick box is selected.","Click on the Advanced... button.","To define the search date by Created date, in the Dates area of the dialog, select the condition from the Created drop-down list and then either type a date in the free text field or select a date from the date picker.","To define the search date by Updated date, in the Dates area of the dialog, select the condition from the Updated drop-down list and then either type a date in the free text field or select a date from the date picker.","To define the search by users (Author, Update author or Locked by user), in the Users area of the dialog, type the user name in the appropriate free text field.","To define the search by Component type, in the Component Type area of the dialog, select the required category from the drop-down list. Use the buttons in the middle to select components you wish to be searched.","&gt;   use this to add a selected component from the left field to the allowed component types","&gt;&gt;  use this to add all components from the left field to the allowed component types","&lt;    use this to remove a selected component from the allowed component types","&lt;&lt;  use this to remove all components from the allowed component types","To define other criteria such as broken, hidden, conflict and locally modified components, in the Others area of the dialog, select the appropriate condition from the drop-down list for any fields you wish to search for.","Click on the Find button.","You may return to the Basic Advanced Search at any time, by clicking on the Basic... button in the Search Window dialog.","The search results will be displayed in the Search Results window, located in the output area of the user interface. ","Use Advanced Search","UseAdvancedSearch.htm");
Page[240]=new Array("The Quick Search function allows the user to search for a word or a phrase. The Quick Search function will locate items in components, action names and in the help system.","A search will be restricted to the components for which the user has permissions.","A Quick Search can be carried out using the Quick Search bar in the Main menu bar.","The Quick Search bar consists of two areas:","Category Selection @ - Click on the magnifying glass icon to display the available search categories.","By default the Quick Search is set to All Categories. The user can confine the search to the following areas:","Components: This category lists search results from the Solution components.","Actions: This category lists search results from the Main menu.","Help: This category lists search results from the Help system.","Quick Search in the system @  - This is a free text field. The user may type a word or phrase in this field.","Search results will display in a grid beneath the Quick Search bar.","The Advanced Search function  and the Where Used query are also available to the user.","Quick Search overview","QuickSearchoverview.htm");
Page[241]=new Array("The Quick Search function allows the user to search for a word or a phrase. The Quick Search function will locate items in components, action names and in the help system.","A Quick Search can be carried out using the Quick Search bar in the Main tool bar. ","To use Quick Search to find a word or a phrase","Load a system. ","You will be unable to carry out a search until you have loaded a solution.","By default the Quick Search is set to All Categories. The search can be defined to certain areas.","Click in the Quick Search field or use CTRL+I to take you to the text field.<br>@ ","Type in the word or the phrase you want to search for.","The results will display in a grid beneath the Quick Search bar.","Select and click on a search result.","Dependant on the category that the result sits within, the appropriate component, action or help topic will display.","Use Quick Search to find a word or phrase","UseQuickSearchtofindawordorphrase.htm");
Page[242]=new Array("The Quick Search function allows the user to search for a word or a phrase. The Quick Search function will locate items in components, action names and in the help system.","A Quick Search can be carried out using the Quick Search bar in the Main tool bar. ","By default the Quick Search is set to All Categories. The user can confine the search to the following areas:","Components: This category lists search results from the solution components.","Actions: This category lists search results from the main menu.","Help: This category lists search results from the Help system..","To search within a defined category","Load a system. ","You will be unable to carry out a search until you have loaded a solution.","By default the Quick Search is set to All Categories. The search can be defined to certain areas.","Click on the Category Selection @ Icon.","From the drop down list, select and click the area for which you wish the search to return results.","Click in the Quick Search field @ .","Type in the word or the phrase you want to search for.","The results will display in a grid beneath the Quick Search bar.","Select and click on a search result.","Dependant on the category that the result sits within, the appropriate component, action or help topic will display.","Use Quick Search in a defined category area","UseQuickSearchinadefinedcategoryarea.htm");
Page[243]=new Array("The Quick Search function allows the user to search for a word or a phrase. The Quick Search function will locate items in components, action names and in the help system.","A Quick Search can be carried out using the Quick Search bar in the Main tool bar. ","Once a search has been carried out, the Quick Search results are displayed grouped by category:","The Quick Search function allows the user to search for a word or a phrase. The Quick Search function will locate items in components, action names and in the help system.","A Quick Search can be carried out using the Quick Search bar in the Main tool bar. ","Once a search has been carried out, the Quick Search results are displayed grouped by category:","Where the Quick Search returns a component name, the result can be selected and initiated in the Main editor, providing the user has the appropriate permission to view that component.<br>If the user does not have permission to open the component, the result will be displayed but the associated open action is disabled. ","Where the search has failed to find a search result, the following will be displayed:","Quick Search results","QuickSearchresults.htm");
Page[244]=new Array("JRE Version","The studio will detect and warn the user if they are not using the supported JRE  (Java Runtime Environment) version.","The following Warning dialog will be displayed:","On receipt of the above warning, the user should check the installed version of JRE. The user may check the Product version, the Java version, the System and the User directory currently being used by clicking on Help in the Main menu bar and selecting About.","If the user has a newer version installed, use of the software can continue, but at the user's risk. The user may click on the OK button to continue.","If the user has an older version installed, it is advisable to install the supported version. ","Please see the Studio Configuration Guide for further information.","IDE Log","The IDE log file contains events that are logged by the applications including errors and information messages.","A user can open a tab in the Output window to view logged information. Please see the Initiate the IDE log help topic for more information.","The IDE Log tab is read only.","Miscellaneous","Miscellaneous.htm");
Page[245]=new Array("The IDE Log file contains events that are logged by the applications including errors and information messages.","A user can open a tab in the Output window to view logged information.","To initiate the IDE Log","In the main system view, click on View in the Main menu bar and select IDE Log.","The Output window is displayed, the IDE Log tab will display within:","Initiate the IDE Log","InitiatetheIDELog.htm");
var PageCount=246;

function search(SearchWord){
var Result="";
var NrRes=0;
Result='<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd">\n';
Result+="<html>\n";
Result+="<head>\n";
Result+="<title>Search Results</title>\n";
Result+="<meta http-equiv='Content-Type' content='text/html; charset=UTF-8'>\n";
Result+='<script language="javascript" type="text/javascript" charset="UTF-8" src="dhtml_search.js"></script>\n';
Result+='<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="stylesheet.css">\n';
Result+="<style type='text/css'>\n";
Result+=".searchDetails {font-family:verdana; font-size:8pt; font-weight:bold}\n";
Result+=".searchResults {font-family:verdana; font-size:8pt}\n";
Result+="</style>\n";
Result+="</head>\n";
Result+="<body onload='javascript:document.SearchForm.SearchText.focus()'>\n";
Result+='<table class="searchDetails" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" width="100%">\n';
Result+='<tr><td>Enter a keyword or phrase</td></tr>';
Result+='<tr><td>';
Result+='<form name="SearchForm" action="javascript:search(document.SearchForm.SearchText.value)">';
if(SearchWord.length>=1){
   while(SearchWord.indexOf("<")>-1 || SearchWord.indexOf(">")>-1 || SearchWord.indexOf('"')>-1){
       SearchWord=SearchWord.replace("<","&lt;").replace(">","&gt;").replace('"',"&quot;");
   }
}
Result+='<input type="text" name="SearchText" size="25" value="' + SearchWord + '" />';
Result+='&nbsp;<input type="submit" value="&nbsp;Go&nbsp;"/></form>';
Result+='</td></tr></table>\n';

if(SearchWord.length>=1){
   SearchWord=SearchWord.toLowerCase();
   this.status="Searching, please wait...";
   Result+="<table border='0' cellpadding='5' class='searchResults' width='100%'>";
   for(j=0;j<PageCount;j++){
       k=Page[j].length-1;
       for(i=0;i<k;i++){
           WordPos=Page[j][i].toLowerCase().indexOf(SearchWord);
           if(WordPos>-1){
               FoundWord=Page[j][i].substr(WordPos,SearchWord.length);
               NrRes++;
               Result+="<tr><td>";
               Result+="<a target='BODY' href='"+Page[j][k]+"'>"+Page[j][k-1].replace(FoundWord,FoundWord.bold())+"</a><br/>\n";

               if(i<k-1){
                   if(Page[j][i].length>350){
                       Result+="..."+Page[j][i].substr(WordPos-100,200+FoundWord.length).replace(FoundWord,FoundWord.bold())+"...\n";
                   }
                   else{
                       Result+=Page[j][i].replace(FoundWord,FoundWord.bold())+"\n";
                   }
               }
               Result+="</td></tr>";
               break;
           }
       }
   }
   Result+="</table>";
   Result+="<p class='searchDetails'>&nbsp;" + NrRes + " result(s) found.</p>";
}

Result+="</body></html>";
this.status="";
this.document.open();
this.document.write(Result);
this.document.close();
}